E["npc:jaina-proudmoore"] = {t="npc",n="Jaina Proudmoore",z="dustwallow",s="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is the ruler of Theramore Isle and the most powerful human sorceress alive. Formerly a star pupil of Dalaran's Kirin Tor, she led the survivors of Lordaeron across the Great Sea and now strives to maintain a fragile peace between the Alliance and the New Horde.",h="Lady Jaina Proudmoore is the ruler of Theramore Isle and the most powerful human sorceress alive.",sec={{t="Flight to Kalimdor",b="The daughter of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras, Jaina showed remarkable aptitude for the arcane at an early age and studied under Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran. During the Third War, she investigated the mysterious Plague of Undeath alongside Prince Arthas Menethil, witnessing firsthand the tragic downfall of Lordaeron. Guided by the warnings of the Prophet Medivh, she rallied an expedition of human survivors and set sail westward to the forgotten continent of Kalimdor. There, her forces forged an unprecedented alliance with Thrall's Horde and the night elves, standing together atop Mount Hyjal to defeat Archimonde and shatter the Burning Legion's invasion.",sp=0},{t="The Lady of Theramore",b="Following the Legion's defeat, Jaina founded the island citadel of Theramore off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, establishing the primary bastion of the Alliance in southern Kalimdor. Her commitment to diplomacy was tested to its limits when her father arrived seeking vengeance against the orcs; Jaina refused to support his war, stepping aside as Thrall's forces slew the Grand Admiral to prevent Kalimdor from plunging into another devastating conflict. Today, she rules Theramore as a steadfast advocate for coexistence, working closely with Warchief Thrall while anchoring the Alliance's presence against rising local tensions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Jaina is the ruler of Theramore Isle and arguably the most gifted human mage alive. She is the daughter of the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras and a former apprentice of Archmage Antonidas in Dalaran.",al={"who is jaina","jaina proudmoore lore","theramore leader"}},{q="Why is Jaina in Kalimdor instead of the Eastern Kingdoms?",a="Before the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, the Prophet Medivh warned Jaina to lead as many people as possible across the sea to Kalimdor. Her expedition survived the journey, fought at Mount Hyjal, and settled the port-fortress of Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why did jaina leave lordaeron","jaina kalimdor","why is theramore here"}},{q="What is Jaina's relationship with the Horde?",a="Jaina maintains an unusual, cautious friendship with Warchief Thrall. After fighting together against the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal, both leaders have strived to keep the peace between their peoples, despite sharp opposition from hardliners on both sides.",al={"is jaina friendly with thrall","jaina and horde","does jaina hate orcs"}},{q="What happened between Jaina and Prince Arthas Menethil?",a="Jaina and Arthas were close companions who shared a romance. They jointly investigated the plague spreading across Lordaeron, but Jaina was horrified by Arthas's descent into ruthlessness—culminating in the purging of Stratholme, where she refused to participate in the slaughter of infected citizens.",al={"jaina and arthas","did jaina love arthas"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Trained under Archmage Antonidas himself, Lady Jaina is widely considered the most powerful living human sorceress, demonstrating the height of Dalaran's arcane mastery.",["faction:Alliance"]="Jaina provides the Alliance with its critical foothold in southern Kalimdor, balancing loyalty to Highlord Bolvar's regency in Stormwind against her desire to avoid war with the neighboring Horde."},kw={"antonidas","arthas","dustwallow","jaina","kirin tor","proudmoore","theramore","thrall"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:dalaran","topic:new-horde","topic:burning-legion","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:medivh","topic:kul-tiras","topic:third-war"},src={"Jaina Proudmoore"}}
E["npc:nat-pagle"] = {t="npc",n="Nat Pagle",z="dustwallow",s="Nat Pagle is widely hailed as the most renowned angler in all of Azeroth, despite claiming he only fishes as an excuse to drink heavily. He makes his home on a secluded inlet in Dustwallow Marsh, where he trains elite anglers from both the Alliance and the Horde who manage to prove their patience.",h="Nat Pagle is widely hailed as the most renowned angler in all of Azeroth, despite claiming he only fishes as...",sec={{t="The Master Angler",b="Though his name is synonymous with angling mastery across the known world, Nat Pagle is remarkably casual about his craft. Having cast lines for several decades, he often admits he has no great reverence for the sport itself, famously calling it little more than a convenient excuse to sit back and drink heavily. Despite this gruff nonchalance, Nat understands aquatic life and the art of angling better than anyone alive, even licensing fishing gear sought out by professionals.",sp=0},{t="A Marshland Hermit",b="Pagle makes his camp on a small spit of land along the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, far from the bustling taverns of the Eastern Kingdoms. He remains fiercely independent and uninterested in the politics of factions, welcoming Alliance travelers sent by trainers like Grimnur Stonebrand as well as Horde aspirants directed to him by Lumak in Orgrimmar. For Nat, anyone willing to scour the corners of the world for rare specimens deserves a lesson in genuine angling.",sp=0},{t="Old Tales and Sea Monsters",b="Pagle has ventured into perilous waters, including an excursion into the ruins of Zul'Gurub where he misplaced his favorite measuring tape and tackle box near the waters prowled by the monstrous hydra Gahz'ranka.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nat Pagle?",a="Nat Pagle is the most famous fisherman in Azeroth. Having angled for decades, he now lives a quiet life along the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, training veteran anglers who have outgrown ordinary trainers.",al={"who is nat","nat pagle lore","who is the fishing guy"}},{q="Where can Nat Pagle be found?",a="He lives on a small spit of land on the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh in Kalimdor, southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nat pagle","nat pagle location","find nat pagle"}},{q="Why does Nat Pagle fish if he says he dislikes it?",a="Pagle has candidly confessed that he views fishing primarily as a respectable, undisturbed excuse to sit by the water and drink heavily for hours at a time.",al={"does nat like fishing","why does nat fish","nat pagle drinking"}},{q="Will Nat Pagle train members of the Horde?",a="Yes. Nat is entirely neutral toward faction rivalries. Horde anglers who reach the upper limits of ordinary skill are sent directly to him by his friend Lumak in Orgrimmar.",al={"is nat alliance only","horde nat pagle","can horde talk to nat"}},{q="What connection does Nat Pagle have to Zul'Gurub?",a="Nat once fished within the ancient troll city of Zul'Gurub, leaving behind his tackle box and prized measuring tape near the waters harboring the great hydra Gahz'ranka.",al={"nat in zg","nat pagle tackle box","nat pagle zul gurub"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Lumak, the fishing trainer in the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar, counts Nat Pagle as a trusted friend and sends promising Horde fishermen south to train with him.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dwarven master anglers such as Grimnur Stonebrand in Ironforge hold Nat in high esteem, sending experienced Alliance fishermen down to Dustwallow Marsh to learn the craft's final secrets."},kw={"artisan fishing","dustwallow marsh","gahz'ranka","grimnur stonebrand","lumak","nat pagle","pagle","pagle's pointe"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","quest:6608","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:ironforge","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Nat Pagle"}}
E["npc:onyxia"] = {t="npc",n="Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="Onyxia is the broodmother of the black dragonflight and the devious daughter of Deathwing. Lurking in her wyrm lair within Dustwallow Marsh, she tends to her burgeoning brood while coordinating with her sinister dragonflight to exert dominance over the mortal realms.",h="Onyxia is the broodmother of the black dragonflight and the devious daughter of Deathwing.",sec={{t="The Broodmother in the Court",b="While her brother Nefarian consolidates his armies within Blackrock Spire, Onyxia pursues power through guile. Taking the guise of Lady Katrana Prestor, she has wormed her way into the highest echelons of Stormwind's nobility. By posing as a trusted adviser to the House of Nobles, she systematically undercuts the kingdom's military efforts, intentionally withholding soldiers and resources from outposts in Westfall, Redridge, and the Burning Steppes to leave mortal realms defenseless.",sp=1},{t="Architect of Ruin",b="Behind the painted smiles of Lady Prestor lies a predatory mastermind. With King Varian missing en route to a peace summit at Theramore, Prestor exerts deep influence over the young boy-king Anduin and ensnares Highlord Bolvar Fordragon, bringing the throne teetering on the edge of her talons.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Katrana Prestor?",a="Lady Katrana Prestor is a Stormwind noblewoman and a trusted advisor at court. With King Varian missing, she stands beside the boy-king Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep, and her counsel carries great weight with the House of Nobles.",al={"prestor identity","who is prestor","katrana prestor real identity"},sp=2,it="identity"},{q="Why does Onyxia target Stormwind?",a="Onyxia aims to bring the kingdom of Stormwind under the black dragonflight's sway, neutralize its military power, and aid her brother Nefarian's dominion over the region.",al={"onyxia goal","why attack stormwind","prestor motive"},sp=2,it="why_here"},{q="Where does Onyxia live?",a="Onyxia's home is a subterranean lair nestled in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh, where she tends to the clutches of her black dragonflight.",al={"where is onyxia","onyxia location","onyxia lair location"},sp=2,it="place"},{q="What is her connection to Nefarian and Deathwing?",a="Onyxia is the daughter of the Aspect Deathwing. She is also the younger sister of Nefarian, working closely with him to restore the black dragonflight's supremacy across Azeroth.",al={"onyxia brother","onyxia father","onyxia family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Onyxia on?",a="Onyxia belongs solely to the black dragonflight and serves the dark designs of her family. Allied closely with her brother Nefarian, she works to rebuild their corrupted flight and subjugate the mortal races. She owes no allegiance to the Alliance or Horde; mortal kingdoms exist only to be manipulated, weakened, and broken to ensure black dragon supremacy.",al={"onyxia side","who does onyxia serve","onyxia faction","onyxia alliance or horde"},it="side",add="fd0ec0c3"},{q="What does Onyxia want?",a="Onyxia seeks to bring the Kingdom of Stormwind under the black dragonflight's sway. She works to weaken its armies and leave the realm defenseless, so that her brood and her brother Nefarian's forces can rise unchallenged.",al={"what does onyxia want","onyxia goal","onyxia motive","what is onyxias plan"},it="wants",add="d77da3f3"},{q="Why is Onyxia so feared?",a="As the daughter of Deathwing and broodmother of the black dragonflight, Onyxia is as deadly in physical might as she is in cunning. Though comparatively small for a mature dragon, her strikes are lightning-quick, and her fiery breath can melt iron within moments. Combined with her insidious talent for weaving deception among mortals, she poses an existential threat to Azeroth.",al={"why is onyxia feared","is onyxia powerful","onyxia reputation"},it="fame",add="ba62a202"}},kw={"anduin wrynn","black dragonflight","bolvar fordragon","deathwing","nefarian","onyxia","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:onyxia-s-lair","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:stormwind","npc:deathwing","topic:house-of-nobles","topic:varian-wrynn","topic:defias-brotherhood"},src={"Onyxia"}}
E["npc:overlord-mok-morokk"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Mok'Morokk",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk is the brute chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, presiding over Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. Originally appointed by Rexxar for his strength, he has become a tyrannical and cowardly ruler who refuses to defend his clan against the black dragonflight.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk is the brute chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, presiding over Brackenwall Village in...",sec={{t="A Tyrant in the Marsh",b="When Rexxar bested the previous chieftain Kor'gall and led the Stonemaul clan in defense of Durotar, he left Mok'Morokk in command, seeing promise in his sheer martial strength. That faith proved misplaced. Mok'Morokk quickly succumbed to the corrupting influence of absolute authority, ruling through intimidation and self-indulgence rather than stewardship. Instead of caring for his kin, he demands unearned tribute, lounges in Brackenwall Village, and bullies anyone who questions his command.",sp=0},{t="The Coward of Brackenwall",b="Mok'Morokk's leadership crumbled entirely when the black dragonflight descended upon the ancestral Stonemaul Village, slaying many ogres and driving the survivors into the muck of Brackenwall. Rather than rallying a counterattack to reclaim their home or avenge the dead, Mok'Morokk forbade any action, cowering from the dragons' wrath. Discontent festers among his advisers, such as the ogre mage Draz'Zilb, who quietly seek outside champions willing to challenge the overlord's shameful reign.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Mok'Morokk is the chieftain of the Stonemaul ogres, currently residing in Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow Marsh. He was named leader by Rexxar but quickly degenerated into a selfish and demanding despot.",al={"who is mok'morokk","brackenwall leader","stonemaul ogre boss"}},{q="How did Mok'Morokk become leader of the Stonemaul clan?",a="During the founding of Durotar, the Champion of the Horde, Rexxar, defeated the clan's previous leader and took command of the Stonemaul. When Rexxar departed to wander the wilderness, he appointed Mok'Morokk as overlord because of his raw physical strength.",al={"how did mok'morokk get in charge","rexxar chose mok'morokk","why is he chieftain"}},{q="Why are the Stonemaul ogres in Brackenwall Village?",a="The Stonemaul ogres originally lived in Stonemaul Village, but black dragons attacked and razed their settlement. The survivors fled north into the swamps to establish Brackenwall Village as a refugee outpost.",al={"why did ogres move to brackenwall","what happened to stonemaul village","black dragon attack ogres"}},{q="Why won't Mok'Morokk fight the black dragonflight?",a="Despite his massive size and fierce reputation, Mok'Morokk is terrified of the dragons. Rather than leading a counterattack to reclaim his clan's ancestral territory, he sits idle in Brackenwall, hoarding tribute and ignoring the cries of his people.",al={"why doesn't mok'morokk fight dragons","is mok'morokk a coward","retake stonemaul"}},{q="Do the other Stonemaul ogres respect Mok'Morokk?",a="The clan grows increasingly resentful of his laziness, cowardice, and bullying. His advisers worry about the future of the Stonemaul under his rule.",al={"do ogres like mok'morokk","draz'zilb mok'morokk","stonemaul rebellion"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are valuable allies sworn to the Horde since Rexxar's campaign, but Mok'Morokk's ineffective and cowardly leadership threatens to leave Brackenwall Village completely vulnerable.",["class:Warrior"]="Mok'Morokk is a textbook example of raw martial strength unguided by honor or courage, demonstrating how easily brute force degenerates into cowardice and tyranny."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","mok'morokk","ogre","overlord","rexxar","stonemaul"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:durotar","npc:onyxia"},src={"Overlord Mok'Morokk"}}
E["npc:tabetha"] = {t="npc",n="Tabetha",z="dustwallow",s="Tabetha is a reclusive, powerful human mage dwelling deep within Dustwallow Marsh at an isolated farmstead in the Quagmire. Far from the politics of Dalaran or Theramore, she instructs aspiring spellcasters and aids those seeking mastery over potent arcane and occult relics.",h="Tabetha is a reclusive, powerful human mage dwelling deep within Dustwallow Marsh at an isolated farmstead in...",sec={{t="Hermit of the Quagmire",b="Hidden away in the sodden expanse of Dustwallow Marsh north of the Stonemaul Ruins, Tabetha lives in a secluded shack alongside her apprentices. Surrounding herself with alchemical vials and ancient tomes, she has deliberately chosen solitude over the academic hierarchies of the Eastern Kingdoms. Despite her remote location, her mastery of the arcane is renowned enough that spellcasters across Kalimdor brave beasts and mire alike to seek her guidance.",sp=0},{t="A Neutral Mentor",b="Tabetha stands notably apart from factional hostilities. While human by birth, she turns away neither Alliance nor Horde initiates who demonstrate the will to learn, providing tutelage to mages and assisting warlocks with dangerous bindings such as the Orb of Orahil. Her past connects her to figures like Menara Voidrender, revealing an extensive history with esoteric magic that transcends simple faction allegiance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Tabetha?",a="Tabetha lives in a secluded shack at Tabetha's Farm, situated deep within the Quagmire in western Dustwallow Marsh, just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tabetha location","where is tabetha","tabetha farm map"}},{q="Is Tabetha hostile to Horde players?",a="No. Despite being human, Tabetha is neutral. She teaches apprentices and aids spellcasters of both the Horde and the Alliance without discrimination.",al={"is tabetha alliance only","can horde talk to tabetha","tabetha faction"}},{q="Why do mages and warlocks seek her out?",a="Tabetha possesses rare knowledge regarding arcane rituals, magical foci, and binding rites. Mages consult her for craft mastery and power trials, while warlocks seek her expertise to cleanse or bind potent artifacts like the Orb of Orahil.",al={"why visit tabetha","tabetha class quest","orb of orahil tabetha"}},{q="What is her connection to Menara Voidrender?",a="Tabetha shares an established history with Menara Voidrender. While their paths have diverged, their mutual understanding of powerful relics and binding magic links them across their respective hermitages.",al={"tabetha and menara","menara voidrender history"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Tabetha is an essential mentor for mid-level mages, testing your grasp of arcane rituals and sending you across dangerous lands like Uldaman to refine your craft.",["class:Warlock"]="Though she practices the arcane, Tabetha's deep understanding of magical relics makes her a critical guide when dealing with dangerous artifacts like the Infernal Orb and the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mage quest","menara voidrender","orb of orahil","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm"},rel={"subzone:tabetha-s-farm","zone:dustwallow","subzone:quagmire","npc:menara-voidrender","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha"}}
E["quest:1132"] = {t="quest",n="Fiora Longears",z="dustwallow",s="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor. Directed by the enthusiastic recruiter Red Jack Flint in Menethil Harbor, travelers take ship across the Great Sea to report to his high elf contact, Fiora Longears, in the inn of Theramore.",h="This errand introduces Alliance adventurers from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed continent of Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Call to the West",b="For many humans, dwarves, and gnomes, the Eastern Kingdoms feel fraught with old conflicts and scarred earth. In the bustling port of Menethil Harbor, the sailor Red Jack Flint spends his days urging adventurous travelers to board a vessel bound across the Great Sea. Describing Kalimdor as an uncharted realm of fortune and opportunity, Flint directs bold wanderers to Theramore to meet his associate, an elf named Fiora Longears.",sp=0},{t="Arrival in Theramore",b="Crossing the ocean brings travelers to Theramore, an Alliance port on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Waiting in the town inn, Fiora Longears receives arrivals recommended by Flint. Trusting Flint's eye for character, Fiora welcomes newly arrived Alliance heroes and prepares to direct them inland toward the ancient forests of Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is a high elf stationed in the inn of Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh. She acts as a welcoming partner and contact for Red Jack Flint, greeting Alliance travelers arriving from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"fiora longears","who is fiora"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Red Jack Flint, an energetic human sailor located in Menethil Harbor along the coast of the Wetlands.",al={"quest giver","where to get fiora longears quest","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="How do I reach Fiora Longears from Menethil Harbor?",a="Board the passenger vessel docked at Menethil Harbor that sails westward across the Great Sea directly to Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"how to get to theramore","ship to theramore","boat from menethil"},gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Fiora Longears?",a="Upon greeting you in Theramore, Fiora commends Flint's recommendation and offers the next leg of your journey, sending you inland to Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","journey to astranaar quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the relationship between Red Jack Flint and Fiora Longears?",a="Flint refers to Fiora as his partner across the sea. While Flint scouts eager adventurers in the Eastern Kingdoms, Fiora receives them in Kalimdor to facilitate Alliance operations and travel inland.",al={"are flint and fiora partners","red jack flint fiora connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why is the Alliance recruiting travelers to Kalimdor?",a="Kalimdor represents vast new territory and resources for the Alliance, as well as a front where night elven allies need assistance protecting their ancestral lands from threats like the Horde and demonic remnants.",al={"why go to kalimdor","why theramore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Red Jack Flint want to send you to Kalimdor?",a="Red Jack Flint sees himself as an agent of opportunity, tasked with inspiring promising adventurers in Menethil Harbor to cross the Great Sea. Bound to the docks himself and longing for ocean voyages, his role is to spot hardy souls and direct them to his high elf partner, Fiora Longears, who helps newcomers find their footing and take up the Alliance's burgeoning efforts across Kalimdor.",al={"red jack flint motive","why send me to fiora","why does jack flint want this done"},it="motive",add="869cd7aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This journey represents the bridge between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elven territories of Kalimdor, uniting the Alliance's eastern and western frontiers.",["race:NightElf"]="Fiora Longears serves as an official welcoming presence for eastern allies arriving at Theramore, preparing them for the ancient wilds of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"theramore","boat","dustwallow marsh","fiora longears","kalimdor","menethil harbor","red jack flint","wetlands"},rel={"npc:red-jack-flint","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:dustwallow","quest:1133","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Red Jack Flint",["end"]="Fiora Longears",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1132},src={"Fiora Longears (quest)"}}
E["quest:1135"] = {t="quest",n="Highperch Venom",z="dustwallow",s="Fiora Longears in Theramore tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying west to the canyons of Thousand Needles. There, atop the elevated bluffs of Highperch, roost dangerous wyverns prized for their exceptionally potent venom.",h="Fiora Longears in Theramore tasks Alliance adventurers with journeying west to the canyons of Thousand...",sec={{t="A Lucrative Expedition",b="While resting in the island port of Theramore, travelers may cross paths with Fiora Longears. While orcs commonly capture and domesticate wyverns as aerial mounts, Fiora points out a far more clandestine trade: the creature's lethal venom. Certain buyers across Kalimdor value fresh venom sacs far more than the beasts themselves, prompting Fiora to recruit hunters willing to brave long distances and precarious heights.",sp=0},{t="The Crags of Highperch",b="The quarry nests west of Dustwallow Marsh, within the towering sandstone mesas of Thousand Needles. At a roost known as Highperch, the local wyverns possess an unusually concentrated toxin. Reaching their nests requires navigating hostile Horde territory and scaling treacherous terrain, where hunters must slay wyverns to extract intact venom sacs before hauling the prize back to Theramore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the wyverns for this quest?",a="The wyverns inhabit Highperch, a tall mesa nestled in the western stretches of Thousand Needles, west of Theramore.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","wyvern location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Fiora Longears?",a="Fiora Longears is an Alliance contact stationed in Theramore off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. She recruits daring adventurers to procure rare and valuable natural reagents from across Kalimdor.",al={"fiora longears","who gives highperch venom"},it="identity"},{q="Why is wyvern venom so valuable?",a="Wyvern venom is extremely potent and prized in select underground circles, apothecaries, and trade networks. While the Horde primarily values wyverns as aerial mounts, their venom glands fetch a handsome price among alchemists and poison-makers.",al={"why wyvern venom","wyvern poison use"},it="power"},{q="Why is a Theramore quest sending me so far west?",a="Fiora is an enterprising dealer seeking exotic specimens that cannot be found in the marshes around Theramore. Highperch in Thousand Needles harbors a distinct, concentrated breed of wyvern not found in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why thousand needles","why send to thousand needles"},it="place"},{q="What happens when you return the venom sacs?",a="Fiora inspects the sacs and notes they are bursting with venom, remarking that such quality usually only comes from young wyverns or fertile females, congratulating you on the hunt.",al={"fiora reaction","quest completion highperch venom"},it="next_step"},{q="Is Highperch safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. Thousand Needles contains heavy Horde presence, centering around nearby settlements like Freewind Post. Scaling Highperch means contending with both wild predators and hostile Horde scouts.",al={"is highperch dangerous","alliance in thousand needles"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Fiora Longears want this done?",a="Fiora has an eye for lucrative commerce and rare reagents. While most know wyverns only as beasts of burden tamed by the Horde, she knows that certain circles pay dearly for potent venom. Harvesting the sacs from Highperch allows her to turn a handsome profit in those specialized markets.",al={"why does fiora want venom","fiora longears motive","why harvest wyvern venom"},it="motive",add="9e43b6cb"},{q="What is the Highperch Venom Sac for?",a="The venom sacs contain the deadly, potent toxin of the wild wyverns that nest upon the heights of Thousand Needles. Highly prized by select alchemists, poisoners, and exotic traders, these bursting sacs fetch an enormous price in markets dealing in rare and dangerous beasts.",al={"what are highperch venom sacs for","venom sac use","why collect venom sacs"},it="item",add="ef763353"},{q="What are the creatures nesting at Highperch?",a="Highperch is a towering mesa in Thousand Needles that serves as a wild roost for native wyverns. Untamed and fiercely territorial, these winged predators glide the desert canyons, using their venomous stingers to fell prey before dragging meals up to their rocky aeries.",al={"what are highperch wyverns","who are you hunting at highperch","what live at highperch"},it="target",add="f9186ab4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues naturally understand the dark allure of exotic toxins. Sourcing pure, unrefined wyvern venom gives an intimate appreciation for Kalimdor's deadliest biological agents.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, sending hunters deep into the arid barrens of Thousand Needles highlights how far trade interests and curious reagents reach outside Ashenvale and Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Venturing into Thousand Needles places Alliance adventurers deep behind enemy lines, right beneath the watchful eyes of the Horde's tauren and orc patrols."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","fiora","highperch","longears","theramore","thousand needles","venom","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1132","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Fiora Longears",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1135,ri={"Highperch Venom Sac"}},src={"Highperch Venom"}}
E["quest:1166"] = {t="quest",n="Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk of the Stonemaul clan is in Brackenwall Village and wants his grog, snuff and strongbox back. He left them behind in a hurry at the clan's old home, and he sends you south to find them.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk of the Stonemaul clan is in Brackenwall Village and wants his grog, snuff and strongbox...",sec={{t="The Overlord's Story",b="Mok'Morokk says Rexxar made him the mighty leader of the Stonemaul clan, and that he keeps his people safe. By his account, big dragons came to the old home and brought fire, so he found the clan a new home here in Dustwallow.",sp=0},{t="Things Left Behind",b="He left the old home so fast that he forgot his belongings: his grog, his snuff and his strongbox. He points you south, to the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins, and is sure they are there. He says he is too busy leading the ogres to go himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk leads the Stonemaul clan from Brackenwall Village. By his own telling, Rexxar made him the clan's mighty leader.",al={"mok'morokk","ogre leader","who is the overlord"}},{q="What happened to the Stonemaul clan's old home?",a="Mok'Morokk says big dragons came and brought fire to the old home, so he found the clan a new home at Brackenwall Village.",al={"why did ogres leave","stonemaul destroyed","dragons attack ogres"}},{q="What does Mok'Morokk want back?",a="He wants his grog, his snuff and his strongbox, which he forgot when he left the old home in a hurry.",al={"mok'morokk items","what things does he want","grog snuff strongbox"}},{q="Where are Mok'Morokk's belongings?",a="He sends you south and is sure the belongings are in the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"where are the items","item locations","find grog and snuff"}},{q="Why doesn't Mok'Morokk fetch his things himself?",a="He says he is too busy leading the ogres to go and get them.",al={"why doesn't mok'morokk go","why send me"}}},kw={"brackenwall","den of flame","dustwallow","grog","mok'morokk","rexxar","snuff","stonemaul","strongbox"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:den-of-flame","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Overlord Mok'Morokk",level="43",id=1166},src={"Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern","Classic quest text: Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern"}}
E["quest:1168"] = {t="quest",n="Army of the Black Dragon",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, the ogre Tharg wants vengeance on the army of the black dragon. Tharg resents Overlord Mok'Morokk for telling the ogres to run rather than fight, and asks you to strike at the Firemane.",h="In Brackenwall Village, the ogre Tharg wants vengeance on the army of the black dragon.",sec={{t="A Grievance of Blood",b="Black dragons killed many ogres, and Tharg's wife was among the dead. Mok'Morokk, whom Rexxar made Overlord, told the survivors to run, and that is how they came to Brackenwall Village. Tharg says ogres are poor at running and ought to fight, and he believes Mok'Morokk cares only for Mok'Morokk. Tharg also says that Mok'Morokk tells all ogres to stay put and keep this place safe.",sp=0},{t="Home in the South",b="Tharg calls the Stonemaul Ruins his home and likes it in the south. Brackenwall Village is not home to him. He wants revenge on the black dragon army and wants the old home back, so he asks you to cut down Firemane Scouts and Firemane Ash Tails among its ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharg?",a="Tharg is an ogre living in Brackenwall Village. His wife was killed by black dragons, and he wants revenge and a return to the Stonemaul Ruins.",al={"tharg lore","who is tharg","tharg dustwallow"}},{q="Why does Tharg dislike Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Rexxar made Mok'Morokk Overlord, but Tharg says he cares more for power than for ogres. When the black dragons killed many ogres, Mok'Morokk told the rest to run, and Tharg thinks ogres should fight.",al={"why tharg hate mok morokk","mok'morokk coward","tharg and mok morokk"}},{q="What happened to Tharg's wife?",a="Black dragons killed her, along with many other ogres. It is the root of Tharg's wish for revenge.",al={"thargs wife","what happened to thargs wife","tharg wife dead"}},{q="Where is the ogres' old home?",a="Tharg calls the Stonemaul Ruins home and likes it in the south. He says Brackenwall Village is not home, and he wants to go back.",al={"stonemaul ogre home","where did ogres come from","stonemaul ruins history"}},{q="Which enemies make up the army of the black dragon?",a="Tharg points you at the Firemane, among them Firemane Scouts and Firemane Ash Tails.",al={"firemane dragonkin","who to kill army of black dragon","firemane enemies"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","firemane","mok'morokk","rexxar","stonemaul","tharg"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Tharg",["end"]="Tharg",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1168},src={"Army of the Black Dragon"}}
E["quest:1169"] = {t="quest",n="Identifying the Brood",z="dustwallow",s="In Brackenwall Village, Draz'Zilb calls Mok'Morokk a craven fool who wallows in power, and says Tharg is wrestling with sorrow and vengeance while vying to lead the clan. Draz'Zilb believes nobody else is concerned with finding who attacked the old home, and asks you for fifteen searing tongues and fifteen searing hearts.",h="In Brackenwall Village, Draz'Zilb calls Mok'Morokk a craven fool who wallows in power, and says Tharg is...",sec={{t="A Voice of Reason",b="Draz'Zilb says Mok'Morokk wallows in power while Tharg wrestles with sorrow and a thirst for vengeance, so by Draz'Zilb's account nobody else is concerned with who is behind the aggression against the old home. Draz'Zilb notes that you may have expected an ogre to speak like a brute.",sp=0},{t="Hearts and Tongues",b="Draz'Zilb wants tongues and hearts taken from whelps and hatchlings, fifteen of each, in order to trace where this evil comes from. From the burnt young of the black dragon army, Draz'Zilb hopes to learn which wretched beast set her young loose in the ogres' home. Knowing the enemy better, the ogres might destroy them for good and take back Stonemaul Village from ruin. Getting Mok'Morokk to leave this swamp, Draz'Zilb adds, will be a great labor of its own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Draz'Zilb?",a="Draz'Zilb is an ogre in Brackenwall Village who speaks in a formal way rather than like a brute, and who wants to find out who is behind the attack on the clan's old home.",al={"drazzilb","ogre mage brackenwall","smart ogre"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb want from the whelps and hatchlings?",a="Draz'Zilb wants fifteen searing tongues and fifteen searing hearts. They are meant to help trace which beast set her young loose in the old home.",al={"searing hearts use","why tongues and hearts","identifying the brood purpose"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb think of the clan's leaders?",a="Draz'Zilb has little respect for Mok'Morokk, calling that ogre a craven fool who lets power go to the head, and speaks of Tharg as someone caught up in sorrow and the hunger for revenge.",al={"mokmorokk problem","tharg and mokmorokk","stonemaul leaders"}}},kw={"black dragon","brackenwall village","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","searing hearts","searing tongues","stonemaul","tharg"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="43",id=1169},src={"Classic quest text: Identifying the Brood"}}
E["quest:1170"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="Draz'Zilb tells of the brood of Onyxia invading Stonemaul Village, and wonders why Deathwing's daughter would come to these lands. You are sent to bring word to Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village.",h="Draz'Zilb tells of the brood of Onyxia invading Stonemaul Village, and wonders why Deathwing's daughter would...",sec={{t="A Troubling Presence",b="Stonemaul Village was invaded by Onyxia's brood, and Draz'Zilb finds it troubling that the daughter of Deathwing would descend upon these lands. Draz'Zilb feels certain Onyxia came for more than a siege on a few ogres, and wants Overlord Mok'Morokk told at once in Brackenwall Village so action can be taken.",sp=0},{t="Word at Brackenwall",b="Mok'Morokk does not welcome the news. The Overlord dislikes dragons, likes it in Brackenwall Village and says there are no dragons here.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Overlord Mok'Morokk?",a="Draz'Zilb sends you, after the brood of Onyxia has invaded Stonemaul Village.",al={"who starts the brood of onyxia","brood of onyxia quest giver"}},{q="Where can Overlord Mok'Morokk be found?",a="You will find Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village.",al={"mok'morokk location","where is mok'morokk","overlord mok'morokk dustwallow"}},{q="Why is Draz'Zilb concerned about Onyxia's brood?",a="Draz'Zilb wonders why Deathwing's daughter would come to these lands, and feels certain it was for more than a siege on a small band of ogres.",al={"why does draz'zilb care about dragons","draz'zilb onyxia concern"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","deathwing","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","onyxia","stonemaul"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:brackenwall-village","npc:onyxia","npc:deathwing","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Overlord Mok'Morokk",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1170},src={"The Brood of Onyxia"}}
E["quest:1171"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk has no wish to hear about dragons. He says there are no black dragons here and sends you back to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village with the news that the ogres are staying.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk has no wish to hear about dragons.",sec={{t="Leave Me Alone",b="After Draz'Zilb sent word of the brood of Onyxia, Overlord Mok'Morokk wants only to be left alone. Mok'Morokk says the ogres stay where they are, that there is no black dragon here, and tells you to go and say so to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="What Draz'Zilb Says",b="Draz'Zilb takes the answer badly and calls the Overlord a lazy coward. Mok'Morokk showed strength while Rexxar was their leader, says Draz'Zilb, but after Rexxar departed, the temptations of power took hold. Mok'Morokk now demands service from the ogres rather than leading them, and Draz'Zilb says something must be done.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Overlord Mok'Morokk refuse to act?",a="Mok'Morokk says there are no black dragons here and wants to be left alone. You are told to carry word to Draz'Zilb that the ogres stay.",al={"why mok'morokk not help","mok'morokk reaction","why no black dragons"}},{q="What comes before this in the storyline?",a="This follows The Brood of Onyxia, in which Draz'Zilb sent you to bring word of the brood to Mok'Morokk.",al={"what comes before this quest","quest chain order"}},{q="Where does this take place?",a="Both Mok'Morokk and Draz'Zilb are in Brackenwall Village.",al={"where is this quest","location"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","brood of onyxia","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","rexxar"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","quest:1170","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","npc:onyxia"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1171},src={"The Brood of Onyxia (2)"}}
E["quest:1172"] = {t="quest",n="The Brood of Onyxia",z="dustwallow",s="Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village does not want a single more whelp of Onyxia to hatch. You are sent to find and destroy the black dragon's eggs near the Wyrmbog, down in the marsh's south.",h="Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village does not want a single more whelp of Onyxia to hatch.",sec={{t="The Eggs in the Wyrmbog",b="Onyxia's brood has been scattered through the Dragonmurk. Draz'Zilb urges haste: the Wyrmbog lies in the south of the marsh, and Draz'Zilb is sure the dragon has made her lair there, with her eggs riddled around it. As long as the land around Stonemaul Village is a nesting place for dragons, the ogres will never take it back, so you are sent to track the eggs down and destroy them.",sp=0},{t="One Last Service",b="With the eggs destroyed, Draz'Zilb says it will be some time before Onyxia can lay more, and thanks you on behalf of the Stonemaul Clan. Then Draz'Zilb asks for one more service. Draz'Zilb judges Mok'Morokk unfit to lead, and Tharg, who would make an excellent leader, is held back by injuries and age. You are asked to drive Mok'Morokk out by force, so that a new leader can bring the clan back to its proper home in the south.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Draz'Zilb, in Brackenwall Village, sends you out against Onyxia's eggs.",al={"who gives the brood of onyxia","quest giver brood of onyxia","drazzilb quest"}},{q="Why must the dragon eggs be destroyed?",a="Draz'Zilb wants no more of Onyxia's whelps to hatch. While the land around Stonemaul Village is a nesting place for dragons, the ogres will never take it back.",al={"why destroy onyxia eggs","why smash eggs","stonemaul village dragon eggs"}},{q="Where are the eggs located?",a="Around the Wyrmbog, in the south of the marsh. Draz'Zilb is sure Onyxia has made her lair there.",al={"where are onyxia eggs","egg of onyxia location","where is wyrmbog"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the broader chain?",a="It comes after Mok'Morokk refused to act on the news of the brood, when you carried his answer back to Draz'Zilb.",al={"brood of onyxia chain","previous quest brood of onyxia","what comes before brood of onyxia 3"}}},kw={"brackenwall","brood of onyxia","dragonmurk","draz'zilb","mok'morokk","onyxia","stonemaul","wyrmbog"},rel={"quest:1170","quest:1171","npc:onyxia","subzone:wyrmbog","subzone:dragonmurk","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Draz'Zilb",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1172},src={"The Brood of Onyxia (3)"}}
E["quest:1173"] = {t="quest",n="Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk",z="dustwallow",s="Overlord Mok'Morokk scoffs at your challenge, promises to crush you and invites you to say when you are ready to be thrashed. Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village had hoped to see Mok'Morokk driven out of the village.",h="Overlord Mok'Morokk scoffs at your challenge, promises to crush you and invites you to say when you are ready...",sec={{t="A Challenge to the Overlord",b="You step up to Overlord Mok'Morokk, who laughs at your nerve, promises to crush you and tells you to speak up when you are ready for your beating. This follows The Brood of Onyxia. Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village expects to see Mok'Morokk chased from the village, and wonders why you would come back just to talk.",sp=0},{t="Word for Draz'Zilb",b="Once the fight is won, Draz'Zilb says Mok'Morokk ran off like a coward, and thanks you for a great service. With Mok'Morokk gone, the ogres can name a new leader who will aid them in taking back their old home for good.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who do you challenge?",a="You challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village. The Overlord answers with a laugh and a boast of crushing you.",al={"who do i fight","challenge target","who is mok'morokk"}},{q="What comes before this challenge?",a="It follows The Brood of Onyxia.",al={"what quest comes before this","prerequisite quest","previous quest"}},{q="Who do you report to after the fight?",a="Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village is the one to report to.",al={"who do i turn this in to","turn in npc","where to go after beating mok'morokk"}},{q="What does Draz'Zilb expect of you?",a="Draz'Zilb expects to see Mok'Morokk chased from the village, and wonders why you would come back just to talk.",al={"why fight mok'morokk","why challenge the overlord","reason for the fight"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","challenge overlord mok'morokk","draz'zilb","dustwallow marsh","mok'morokk","stonemaul"},rel={"npc:overlord-mok-morokk","quest:1172","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Overlord Mok'Morokk",["end"]="Draz'Zilb",level="45",id=1173},src={"Classic quest text: Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk"}}
E["quest:1177"] = {t="quest",n="Hungry!",z="dustwallow",s="Mudcrush Durtfeet, an ogre in northern Dustwallow Marsh, is hungry. Mud wants you to go bash the fishy Mirefin and bring back their heads, or Mud will eat you instead.",h="Mudcrush Durtfeet, an ogre in northern Dustwallow Marsh, is hungry.",sec={{t="A Hungry Ogre",b="Mudcrush Durtfeet is a big ogre and says so plainly. Mud is hungry and has a simple bargain: go bash the fishy Mirefin and bring Mud their heads as food. Feed Mud, or Mud will eat you.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mudcrush Durtfeet?",a="Mudcrush Durtfeet is a big ogre in northern Dustwallow Marsh who goes by Mud. Mud is hungry and wants food.",al={"mudcrush durtfeet","who is mudcrush","ogre in dustwallow"}},{q="What does Mudcrush Durtfeet want to eat?",a="Mud wants Mirefin heads, brought from the fishy Mirefin that you are told to bash.",al={"mudcrush food","what does the ogre want","hungry quest food"}},{q="What happens if you refuse to feed him?",a="Mud makes it plain: feed Mud or Mud will eat you.",al={"mudcrush threat","will mudcrush eat me"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","fishy","hungry!","mirefin heads","mudcrush durtfeet","ogre"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Mudcrush Durtfeet",["end"]="Mudcrush Durtfeet",level="36",id=1177},src={"Hungry!"}}
E["quest:1201"] = {t="quest",n="Theramore Spies",z="dustwallow",s="The truce between Horde and Alliance is an uneasy one, with skirmishes and covert deeds on both sides. Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village wants the Alliance infiltrators east of the village hunted down and slain.",h="The truce between Horde and Alliance is an uneasy one, with skirmishes and covert deeds on both sides.",sec={{t="Spies East of the Village",b="Alliance infiltrators have settled in east of Brackenwall Village, watching it and sending word of Horde movements to Theramore. Nazeer Bloodpike, the local spymaster, will not stand for it. You are sent to find the infiltrators and kill them, so that their superiors know such spies are unwelcome.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the death of the Theramore infiltrators?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike, the local spymaster in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gives quest theramore spies","nazeer bloodpike spy quest","who starts theramore spies"}},{q="Where are the infiltrators hiding?",a="East of Brackenwall Village, on the islands.",al={"theramore infiltrators location","where to find theramore spies","infiltrator locations dustwallow"}},{q="Why are the spies watching Brackenwall Village?",a="They watch the village and pass word of Horde movements back to Theramore.",al={"why are humans spying on brackenwall","brackenwall village spies motive"}},{q="What comes after dealing with the spies?",a="The next step in the story is The Theramore Docks.",al={"theramore spies follow up","what quest comes after theramore spies"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","infiltrators","nazeer bloodpike","spies","theramore"},rel={"quest:1202","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1201},src={"Theramore Spies"}}
E["quest:1202"] = {t="quest",n="The Theramore Docks",z="dustwallow",s="Two spies were sent to steal papers from a ship at Theramore, but were found out and had to cast the papers into the sea. Now Nazeer Bloodpike charges you with finding them.",h="Two spies were sent to steal papers from a ship at Theramore, but were found out and had to cast the papers...",sec={{t="Papers in the Water",b="After you dealt with the Theramore spies, Nazeer Bloodpike has another matter for you. Two spies were sent to take papers from a ship by the Theramore docks. They got them, were discovered, and had to throw their haul into the sea. One of them got away but could not retrieve it, and came back to report the failure.",sp=0},{t="Beneath the Docks",b="The papers lie inside a footlocker, somewhere under the water by the Theramore docks. You are sent to find the Captain's Documents and bring them to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village. Nazeer says they matter greatly to the Alliance's stability, and so to the Horde's security.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Theramore Isle?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike, in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gives the quest","where does this quest start","quest giver"}},{q="What are you looking for beneath the docks?",a="A footlocker in the waters beneath the Theramore docks, holding the Captain's Documents.",al={"what do i need to find","what item is in the water","docks objective"}},{q="Why were the documents thrown into the water?",a="Two spies stole the papers from a ship at the docks, but they were discovered and had to cast them into the sea. One escaped without them.",al={"why are the papers in the ocean","how did the footlocker get there","why did the spies drop it"}},{q="Why does the Horde want these documents?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike says they matter greatly to the Alliance's stability, and so to the security of the Horde.",al={"why are the papers important","what is in the documents","why does bloodpike want them"}},{q="What comes before this in the storyline?",a="It follows Theramore Spies, in which you hunted the infiltrators east of Brackenwall Village.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest","what leads to this"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","captain's documents","docks","dustwallow marsh","footlocker","nazeer bloodpike","spies","theramore"},rel={"quest:1201","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1202},src={"The Theramore Docks"}}
E["quest:1203"] = {t="quest",n="Jarl Needs a Blade",z="dustwallow",s="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl, in Dustwallow Marsh, has cutting to do and will not say what. Jarl wants a certain blade, a moonsteel broadsword, and does not want you to dawdle.",h="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl, in Dustwallow Marsh, has cutting to do and will not say what.",sec={{t="A Certain Blade",b="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl has cutting to do, and cannot say what is to be cut. Jarl needs a particular blade, which some call a moonsteel broadsword and Jarl calls a swing blade. You might find one in town, or a blacksmith might make one special. Jarl warns you not to sleep on it, since what is to be cut will not keep forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the blade?",a="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl, who is found in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives jarl needs a blade","who is jarl","swamp eye jarl"}},{q="What weapon does Jarl require?",a="A moonsteel broadsword, which Jarl calls a swing blade.",al={"what sword does jarl want","jarl weapon","which blade does jarl need"}},{q="Why does Jarl need a blade so urgently?",a="Jarl has cutting to do, cannot say what is to be cut, and warns that it will not keep forever.",al={"why does jarl need a blade","what is jarl cutting","jarl purpose"}},{q="Where does Jarl suggest finding the sword?",a="Jarl says you might find one in town, or talk to a blacksmith who can make it special.",al={"how to get moonsteel broadsword for jarl","where to find blade for jarl"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","jarl","moonsteel broadsword","swamp eye jarl","swing blade"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1203},src={"Jarl Needs a Blade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1204"] = {t="quest",n="Mudrock Soup and Bugs",z="dustwallow",s="In Theramore, Morgan Stern is working on a dish called Mudrock Soup and Bugs, which could be the next big thing at the inns of Stormwind City. Morgan Stern doubts they would survive a long trek through Dustwallow Marsh, and so asks you to gather tongues from the Mudrock turtles.",h="In Theramore, Morgan Stern is working on a dish called Mudrock Soup and Bugs, which could be the next big...",sec={{t="A Dish in the Making",b="Morgan Stern is working on a dish called Mudrock Soup and Bugs, and still needs the major ingredients. A long trek through Dustwallow Marsh is more than Morgan Stern expects to survive, so you are asked to do some hunting. First come the tongues of Mudrock turtles.",sp=0},{t="Forked Tongues",b="Mudrocks roam the coast, mostly around the bay. Morgan Stern wants no ordinary tongues. Word has reached Morgan Stern that some Mudrocks have forked tongues, and that these carry a distinct flavor wanted in the dish.",sp=0},{t="Toward the Table",b="Morgan Stern will try different ways of cooking the tongues, searching for what best brings out their taste. The hope is a dish fit to be served at the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the turtle tongues?",a="Morgan Stern, in Theramore, who is working on a dish called Mudrock Soup and Bugs.",al={"who starts mudrock soup and bugs","morgan stern theramore"}},{q="Where can the Mudrock turtles be found?",a="Along the coast of Dustwallow Marsh, mostly around the bay.",al={"mudrock turtle location","where are mudrocks"}},{q="Why does Morgan Stern want forked tongues specifically?",a="Morgan Stern has heard they carry a distinct flavor, and wants that flavor in the dish.",al={"why forked tongues","forked mudrock tongues reason"}},{q="Why won't Morgan Stern gather the ingredients in person?",a="Morgan Stern does not think they would survive a long trek through Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"why doesnt morgan stern hunt","morgan stern marsh"}},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="The next step is called ... and Bugs.",al={"next quest after mudrock soup","mudrock soup follow up"}}},kw={"blue recluse","bugs","dustwallow marsh","forked tongues","morgan stern","mudrock","soup","theramore"},rel={"quest:1258","zone:dustwallow","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Morgan Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1204},src={"Mudrock Soup and Bugs"}}
E["quest:1206"] = {t="quest",n="Jarl Needs Eyes",z="dustwallow",s="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at Swamplight Manor wants 40 unpopped Darkmist eyes, because Darkmist eye juice is smooth and salty. The spiders live in Darkmist Cavern, west of the manor.",h="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at Swamplight Manor wants 40 unpopped Darkmist eyes, because Darkmist eye juice is smooth...",sec={{t="A Taste for Spider Eyes",b="Following Soothing Spices, Jarl turns to eye juice, which is good for drinking. Most critters carry a mere pair of eyes, whereas spiders carry a great many, and Jarl finds Darkmist eye juice tasty. The Darkmist spiders live in Darkmist Cavern, west of the manor, and Jarl muses over whether the cave gave the spiders their name or the reverse.",sp=0},{t="A Feast for Jarl",b="Jarl cheers at the arrival of the eyes, calling them tasty. Jarl advises saving for last any that stare back when stared at, since they give a person something for company in the swamp. Jarl then greets the little eyes, tastes them and declares them like gooey, salty chicken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the spider eyes?",a="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl asks for them, at Swamplight Manor in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives this quest","jarl quest giver","swamp eye jarl"}},{q="Why does Jarl want spider eyes?",a="Jarl likes eye juice for drinking and finds Darkmist eye juice smooth and salty. Most critters have only two eyes, while spiders have a great many.",al={"why spider eyes","what does jarl do with eyes","eye juice"}},{q="Where are the Darkmist spiders?",a="Jarl places the Darkmist spiders in Darkmist Cavern, to the west of Swamplight Manor.",al={"darkmist cavern location","where are darkmist spiders","where to find eyes"}},{q="How many eyes does Jarl want?",a="Jarl wants 40 unpopped Darkmist eyes.",al={"how many eyes","eye count"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="Soothing Spices came first.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what leads to this"}}},kw={"darkmist","darkmist cavern","dustwallow marsh","jarl","spider eyes","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor"},rel={"subzone:swamplight-manor","subzone:darkmist-cavern","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1206},src={"Classic quest text: Jarl Needs Eyes"}}
E["quest:1218"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Spices",z="dustwallow",s="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl loves cooking, swamp style, and needs soothing spice for a stew. Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh asks you to bring three Soothing Spices.",h="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl loves cooking, swamp style, and needs soothing spice for a stew.",sec={{t="Spice for the Pot",b="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl is fond of cooking in the swamp manner, with fried green frog legs among the dishes. A stew is planned, and for it Jarl needs soothing spice. Whoever brings it will be given a share. Jarl wants three Soothing Spices, and wonders whether you like stew.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the soothing spices?",a="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl, who is found in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"who gives soothing spices","quest giver soothing spices","swamp eye jarl spices"}},{q="What does Swamp Eye Jarl intend to cook with the spices?",a="A stew. Jarl is fond of swamp cooking, fried green frog legs for one, and plans to share the stew with you.",al={"what does jarl make","what stew does jarl make","jarl food"}},{q="How many spices does Jarl need?",a="Jarl asks for three Soothing Spices.",al={"how many soothing spices","soothing spices count","soothing spices requirement"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","frog legs","soothing spices","stew","swamp eye jarl"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",["end"]="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl",level="35",id=1218},src={"Soothing Spices (quest)"}}
E["quest:1219"] = {t="quest",n="The Orc Report",z="dustwallow",s="Sifting through loose dirt in Dustwallow Marsh, you come upon an orc's severed hand clutching a tube carved from bone. Inside lies a dirt-stained parchment in Orcish script, which looks important. It is meant for a Theramore Lieutenant.",h="Sifting through loose dirt in Dustwallow Marsh, you come upon an orc's severed hand clutching a tube carved...",sec={{t="A Hand in the Dirt",b="In the loose dirt lies an orc's severed hand, gripping a tube carved from bone. Inside is a parchment stained with dirt and the writing is Orcish, which seems significant. A Theramore Lieutenant is the one to show it to.",sp=0},{t="The Lieutenant's Verdict",b="The lieutenant admits to reading Orcish poorly, yet takes the parchment for an orc spy's report.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is hidden in the loose dirt?",a="Sifting through it turns up an orc's severed hand clutching a tube carved from bone, with a dirt-stained parchment inside.",al={"what do you find in loose dirt","loose dirt item","orc hand in dustwallow"}},{q="Who should get the parchment?",a="A Theramore Lieutenant.",al={"where do I take the report","who gets the spy report","theramore lieutenant location"}},{q="What language is the parchment written in?",a="The writing is Orcish, and it seems significant.",al={"parchment language","can I read the parchment"}}},kw={"bone tube","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","orc report","theramore lieutenant"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Theramore Lieutenant",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1219},src={"Classic quest text: The Orc Report"}}
E["quest:1220"] = {t="quest",n="Captain Vimes",z="dustwallow",s="Lieutenant Aden sends you with the orc report you found to Captain Garran Vimes, who reads orcish better than most. News of Horde spies near Theramore is to go with it.",h="Lieutenant Aden sends you with the orc report you found to Captain Garran Vimes, who reads orcish better than...",sec={{t="A Report for the Captain",b="Lieutenant Aden thinks the orc report you found belongs in the hands of Captain Garran Vimes, who reads orcish better than most. Aden also wants the captain told that Horde spies are lurking close to Theramore. You will find Vimes at the barracks on Theramore Isle's northeastern side.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Captain Vimes?",a="Lieutenant Aden, who wants the captain to see the orc report you found.",al={"who starts captain vimes","where do i get captain vimes"}},{q="Where is Captain Garran Vimes located?",a="At the barracks, on Theramore Isle's northeastern side.",al={"where is captain vimes","captain vimes location","vimes barracks"}},{q="Why does Captain Vimes need to see the report?",a="Aden says Vimes reads orcish better than most, and should hear that Horde spies are close to Theramore.",al={"why captain vimes","why does vimes need the report"}}},kw={"captain vimes","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","lieutenant aden","orc report","spy's report","theramore","theramore isle"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:horde"},m={start="Lieutenant Aden",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1220},src={"Captain Vimes"}}
E["quest:1222"] = {t="quest",n="Stinky's Escape",z="dustwallow",s="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is out in the swamp, where Morgan Stern, a cook in Theramore, sent him to gather bogbean leaves. Critters have surrounded him, and he asks you to help him out and watch his back while he looks for a bogbean plant. Afterward, Morgan Stern in Theramore is the one to see.",h="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is out in the swamp, where Morgan Stern, a cook in Theramore, sent him to gather bogbean...",sec={{t="Surrounded",b="Ignatz is relieved to meet someone who does not see him as a meal. He says Morgan Stern, a cook, is working on a new recipe and sent him out to collect bogbean leaves, which Ignatz guesses Stern finds tasty. While looking for a plant, Ignatz was surrounded, and he asks you to help him out and guard his back as he searches.",sp=0},{t="A Cook Waiting",b="Morgan Stern in Theramore is anxious: Ignatz set off for the swamp a while ago and is still not back.",sp=0},{t="Thanks from the Cook",b="Stern says Ignatz came by with the bogbean leaves and told of how you got him through his trouble. As thanks, Stern will ask an uncle to give you a feast when you next visit the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Stinky\" Ignatz?",a="\"Stinky\" Ignatz was sent into the swamp by the cook Morgan Stern to gather bogbean leaves.",al={"stinky ignatz","who is stinky","ignatz dustwallow"}},{q="Why is Ignatz in trouble?",a="While he looked for a bogbean plant, the critters around him closed in and surrounded him.",al={"why is stinky trapped","ignatz stranded","why is stinky in dustwallow"}},{q="What are bogbean leaves for?",a="Morgan Stern is working on a new recipe and sent Ignatz for the leaves. Ignatz guesses Stern finds them tasty.",al={"bogbean leaves","what are bogbeans","bogbean plant"}},{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is a cook in Theramore who is working on a new recipe.",al={"morgan stern theramore","who is morgan stern","cook morgan stern"}}},kw={"blue recluse","bogbean","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","stinky ignatz","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","quest:1271"},m={start="\"Stinky\" Ignatz",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1222},src={"Classic quest text: Stinky's Escape"}}
E["quest:1238"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Report",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a spy's report bound for Brackenwall Village. An orc's severed hand grips a bone tube holding a dirt-stained account of weeks spent watching Theramore.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a spy's report bound for Brackenwall Village.",sec={{t="A Hand in the Dirt",b="You find an orc's severed hand in loose dirt, its fingers closed around a tube carved from bone. Inside lies a dirt-stained parchment. It reports on Theramore after weeks of spying and is meant for Nazeer Bloodpike, the orcs' spymaster at Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Word from the Spymaster",b="Nazeer Bloodpike names Marg Nighteye as the report's author. Marg was an agent stationed outside Theramore to watch the city. This is Marg's latest report, and perhaps the last. From what you tell him, Bloodpike fears Marg met an end in the swamp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the report found?",a="You find the report in loose dirt in Dustwallow Marsh, clutched by a severed orc hand.",al={"where is the report","lost report location","how to start the lost report"}},{q="What is the report about?",a="An orc wrote the report after spying on Theramore for weeks.",al={"what is in the report","what does the spy report say","parchment contents"}},{q="Who gets the report?",a="The report goes to Nazeer Bloodpike, the orcs' spymaster at Brackenwall Village.",al={"who do i turn the report in to","lost report turn in","where to bring spy report"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","nazeer bloodpike","spy report","the lost report","theramore"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1238},src={"Classic quest text: The Lost Report"}}
E["quest:1239"] = {t="quest",n="The Severed Head",z="dustwallow",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a male orc's severed head. Bring it to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, you uncover a male orc's severed head.",sec={{t="A Grim Find",b="Your digging turns up a male orc's head, ragged where it was cut from the neck. Its lips curl in a snarl, and dark eyes glare defiantly. Bring the head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Nazeer Looks Closer",b="Nazeer Bloodpike recognizes Marg Nighteye's head at once, though he had feared Marg was dead. The ragged wound leaves him wondering whether a weapon made the cut or a beast killed the agent. Nazeer wants to solve the mystery and learn whether the Alliance was behind Marg's death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do you bring the severed head?",a="Bring the severed head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",al={"where to turn in severed head","severed head turn in","who takes the head"}},{q="What does the head look like?",a="It is a male orc's head, ragged where it was cut from the neck, with lips drawn in a snarl and dark eyes glaring defiantly.",al={"what is in the loose dirt","defiant orc head","severed head description"}},{q="What comes after the severed head?",a="The next step is The Troll Witchdoctor.",al={"next quest after severed head","severed head followup"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","defiant orc head","dustwallow marsh","loose dirt","marg nighteye","nazeer bloodpike","severed head"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","quest:1240","topic:alliance"},m={start="Loose Dirt",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1239},src={"The Severed Head"}}
E["quest:1240"] = {t="quest",n="The Troll Witchdoctor",z="dustwallow",s="Nazeer Bloodpike means to learn what happened around Marg Nighteye's death, and says only the witch-magic of trolls can tell. You carry Marg's head to Kin'weelay at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",h="Nazeer Bloodpike means to learn what happened around Marg Nighteye's death, and says only the witch-magic of...",sec={{t="Witch-Magic of the Trolls",b="After the severed head turned up, Nazeer Bloodpike insists the events around Marg's death must be known, and that only troll witch-magic can reveal them. Marg's head is to go to Kin'weelay in Stranglethorn Vale, at Grom'gol Base Camp. Among the Darkspear trolls no witchdoctor is mightier than Kin'weelay, and Nazeer reckons that Kin'weelay, if anyone, can reach Marg's spirit.",sp=0},{t="Words at Grom'gol",b="Kin'weelay senses an angry spirit about you as you arrive. Looking at the head, the witchdoctor sees that the orc's spirit is bound in this world, boiling with rage over a duty left undone, and proposes to have words with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why must Marg Nighteye's head be taken to Stranglethorn Vale?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike says the only way to learn the events of Marg's death is the witch-magic of trolls, and Kin'weelay is at Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"why go to stranglethorn","why grom'gol","why kin'weelay"}},{q="Who is Kin'weelay?",a="The mightiest witchdoctor among the Darkspear trolls, found at Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who is the witchdoctor","witchdoctor kin'weelay"}},{q="What comes after this step?",a="The next step is Marg Speaks.",al={"what quest is next","after the troll witchdoctor"}}},kw={"darkspear witchdoctor","defiant orc head","grom'gol base camp","kin'weelay","marg nighteye","nazeer bloodpike","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:kin-weelay","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","zone:stranglethorn","quest:1239","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Kin'weelay",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1240},src={"The Troll Witchdoctor"}}
E["quest:1251"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="The Shady Rest Inn lies burned out, and one of the few parts still standing is a crumbling chimney. A shield blackened by the flames is fixed to its brick. Krog at Brackenwall Village is the one to show it to.",h="The Shady Rest Inn lies burned out, and one of the few parts still standing is a crumbling chimney.",sec={{t="A Shield on the Chimney",b="Fire tore through the Shady Rest Inn, and little of it remains. Fixed to the crumbling chimney is an iron shield charred black, and it can be worked free of the brick. Krog at Brackenwall Village is the one to bring it to, and will ask whether it counts as evidence from the inn's remains.",sp=0},{t="What Krog Makes of It",b="Krog grants that humans have odd tastes in decoration, yet doubts anyone would hang a plain iron shield over a fireplace. Krog suspects whoever set the inn ablaze left it there, perhaps as a warning or a threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the black shield found?",a="It is fixed to the chimney of the burned Shady Rest Inn, one of the few remnants of the building.",al={"black shield location","where is shield","shady rest inn shield"}},{q="Who gets the shield?",a="Krog, at Brackenwall Village, is the one to bring it to.",al={"who wants the black shield","where to turn in shield","krog location"}},{q="Can the shield be taken from the chimney?",a="Yes, it can be worked loose from the chimney's brick.",al={"can i remove the shield","take shield off chimney"}}},kw={"black shield","blackened iron shield","brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","krog","shady rest inn"},rel={"quest:1321","subzone:shady-rest-inn","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Black Shield",["end"]="Krog",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1251},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1252"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="Something gleams beneath the rubble: a badge bearing Theramore's sign, a golden anchor over white enamel, with the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe embossed under the anchor. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore is the one to bring it to.",h="Something gleams beneath the rubble: a badge bearing Theramore's sign, a golden anchor over white enamel...",sec={{t="A Glint in the Rubble",b="Something gleams beneath the rubble. Brushing off the ash and debris reveals a badge showing the sign of Theramore, with Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name embossed below it. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore should see it, and will ask what turned up in the ruins of the Shady Rest Inn.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Reply",b="Vimes says a guard's badge brought in is never good news. Some guards fall in battle, and Vimes must carry the word to their grieving families. For others, nobody ever learns what became of them, and sometimes the truth is worse still.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the badge found?",a="It lies beneath rubble, caked in ash and debris. Captain Garran Vimes will ask what turned up in the ruins of the Shady Rest Inn.",al={"badge location","where to find reethe badge","shady rest inn badge"}},{q="Whose name is on the badge?",a="The name embossed beneath the anchor is Lieutenant Paval Reethe.",al={"who is paval reethe","name on badge","who lost the badge"}},{q="Who gets the badge?",a="Captain Garran Vimes, in Theramore, is who should see it.",al={"who do i give the badge to","where to turn in badge","captain garran vimes location"}},{q="What does the badge look like?",a="A gold anchor over white enamel, which is the sign of Theramore.",al={"theramore symbol","guard badge appearance","what does the badge look like"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","paval reethe","shady rest inn","theramore guard badge"},rel={"quest:1259","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Theramore Guard Badge",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1252},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1253"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="An iron shield, blackened by fire, is fixed to the crumbling chimney of the burned Shady Rest Inn. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore is waiting on evidence from the inn's site.",h="An iron shield, blackened by fire, is fixed to the crumbling chimney of the burned Shady Rest Inn.",sec={{t="A Shield on the Chimney",b="The Shady Rest Inn burned, and one of the few parts left standing is a crumbling chimney. A fire-blackened iron shield is fixed to its brick, and it can be removed. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore wants evidence from the inn's site.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Verdict",b="Vimes says he is no expert on how arms and armor are made, only on how they are used. To the captain, the shield looks as ordinary as any, apart from the damage left by the fire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the black shield located?",a="Fixed to the brick of the crumbling chimney, among the few parts of the burned Shady Rest Inn still standing.",al={"where is the shield","black shield location","find black shield"}},{q="Who wants evidence from the Shady Rest Inn?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore, who is waiting for proof from the ruins of the inn.",al={"who wants the shield","shady rest investigator","who is garran vimes"}}},kw={"black shield","chimney","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","iron shield","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Black Shield",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1253},src={"The Black Shield (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:1258"] = {t="quest",n="... and Bugs",z="dustwallow",s="Morgan Stern in Theramore is working on a recipe that could become the next food craze in Stormwind. With the Mudrock tongues already in hand, the next part of the dish calls for the shelled legs of a giant crab, and only pristine, unscarred ones will do.",h="Morgan Stern in Theramore is working on a recipe that could become the next food craze in Stormwind.",sec={{t="Legs Without a Scratch",b="Morgan Stern wants the shell of the crab leg to be a key part of how the dish looks, so every leg has to be pristine and unscarred. An adult crab might carry only one or two such legs, and the research calls for a lot of them. The Muckshells of Dustwallow Marsh will not do. Only the crabs of the faraway Swamp of Sorrows will suit, so a journey lies ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is working in Theramore on a new recipe that might become the next food craze in Stormwind.",al={"who is morgan stern","morgan stern theramore","who gives and bugs"}},{q="Where do the crab legs come from?",a="Not from Dustwallow Marsh, where the Muckshells are no good for the dish. Morgan Stern points to the Swamp of Sorrows, far away, for crabs that will do.",al={"where to find crawler legs","where are spiny rock crawlers","crawler legs location"}},{q="Why do the crab legs need to be pristine?",a="The shell is a key part of how the dish is presented, so Morgan Stern wants legs with no scars on them.",al={"why pristine crawler legs","why unscarred legs","crawler leg presentation"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Mudrock Soup and Bugs, the first part of the work you did for Morgan Stern's new recipe.",al={"previous quest and bugs","mudrock soup and bugs prerequisite"}}},kw={"crawler legs","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","mudrock soup and bugs","pristine crawler leg","stormwind","theramore","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"quest:1204","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Morgan Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1258},src={"... and Bugs"}}
E["quest:1259"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="Captain Garran Vimes does not recognize the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe, and sends you to Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore, who looks after the records of the Theramore guard.",h="Captain Garran Vimes does not recognize the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe, and sends you to Adjutant Tesoran...",sec={{t="Who Is Reethe?",b="Captain Garran Vimes cannot place the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Adjutant Tesoran keeps the records of the Theramore guard, covering its people as well as its equipment, and Vimes expects a look through those books to show who Reethe is.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find out about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes, who does not recognize the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe.",al={"who starts lieutenant paval reethe","reethe quest giver","who gives reethe quest"}},{q="Who keeps the Theramore guard's records?",a="Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore keeps them, covering the guard's people and its equipment.",al={"where is adjutant tesoran","theramore records keeper","who has the guard books"}},{q="What can Adjutant Tesoran tell you?",a="Vimes expects Tesoran's books to show who Reethe is.",al={"what does tesoran know","tesoran books"}}},kw={"adjutant tesoran","captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","paval reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1252","quest:1285","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Adjutant Tesoran",level="40",id=1259},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1260"] = {t="quest",n="Morgan Stern",z="dustwallow",s="Angus Stern of the Blue Recluse in Stormwind is putting together a new menu of rural dishes with a bayou theme. Angus has a nephew, Morgan, who was sent to Theramore to gather recipes from the locals, and wants word of what Morgan has found so far.",h="Angus Stern of the Blue Recluse in Stormwind is putting together a new menu of rural dishes with a bayou...",sec={{t="A Bayou Menu",b="Angus Stern believes the customers of the Blue Recluse will love a menu of rural dishes in the bayou style. To build it, Angus sent nephew Morgan off to Theramore, a city beside Dustwallow Marsh, to gather the locals' recipes. The trip is too long for Angus to make, so a young traveler like you is wanted to go and speak with Morgan.",sp=0},{t="What Morgan Has to Say",b="When you find Morgan Stern in Theramore, you hear that the recipe research has turned up some leads, but help is needed to follow them. The helper has to be someone willing to get their feet wet.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Morgan Stern?",a="Morgan Stern is the nephew of Angus Stern of the Blue Recluse. Morgan was sent to Theramore to gather recipes from the locals.",al={"who is morgan stern","morgan stern lore","angus stern nephew"}},{q="Why does Angus Stern want to reach Morgan?",a="Angus is developing a new menu of rural dishes with a bayou theme for the Blue Recluse, and wants to know what Morgan has found so far.",al={"why send to theramore","blue recluse menu","angus stern quest"}},{q="Where can Morgan Stern be found?",a="Morgan is in Theramore, the city beside Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where is morgan stern","morgan stern location","theramore chef location"}}},kw={"angus stern","bayou","blue recluse","dustwallow marsh","morgan stern","stormwind","theramore"},rel={"quest:1204","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Angus Stern",["end"]="Morgan Stern",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1260},src={"Morgan Stern (quest)"}}
E["quest:1261"] = {t="quest",n="Marg Speaks",z="dustwallow",s="From beyond death, Marg tells of the muckshell that killed Marg and of a duty still undone. Marg asks you to find that muckshell, recover the jeweled pendant stolen from Alliance soldiers and carry it to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",h="From beyond death, Marg tells of the muckshell that killed Marg and of a duty still undone.",sec={{t="What Marg Saw Near Theramore",b="Near Theramore, Marg spotted Alliance soldiers camped on the beach. One of them wore a pendant studded with more gems than a soldier could ever pay for. That night Marg snuck into the camp and stole it, but a muckshell crab-man killed Marg on the way back to base. Now Marg asks you to find that muckshell, recover the pendant and bring it to Nazeer in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="What Nazeer Makes of It",b="Nazeer is startled to learn that a soldier of Stormwind wore this pendant. You have uncovered the secret of how Marg died, yet the pendant is a new mystery, and Nazeer warns it may have dire effects on both the Alliance and the Horde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Marg and how did Marg die?",a="Marg stole a jeweled pendant from Alliance soldiers camped near Theramore, then was killed by a muckshell crab-man on the way back to base.",al={"how did marg die","who is marg","marg story"}},{q="Where did the jeweled pendant come from?",a="A soldier in an Alliance camp on the beach near Theramore wore it, studded with far more gems than a soldier could pay for. Marg snuck in that night and stole it.",al={"where did the pendant come from","who had the pendant","marg pendant origin"}},{q="Who receives the recovered pendant?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike, in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gets the pendant","where do i take the pendant","nazeer bloodpike pendant"}},{q="What comes directly before this quest?",a="It follows The Troll Witchdoctor.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before marg speaks"}}},kw={"bloodpike","brackenwall","marg","muckshell","nazeer","pendant","stormwind","theramore"},rel={"quest:1240","quest:1262","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Bubbling Cauldron",["end"]="Nazeer Bloodpike",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1261},src={"Marg Speaks"}}
E["quest:1262"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Zor",z="dustwallow",s="Nazeer Bloodpike finds it strange that common soldiers were carrying the jeweled pendant Marg stole. Calling it a noble's piece, Nazeer sends you to Orgrimmar with it, to Zor Lonetree, who is well schooled in Alliance politics.",h="Nazeer Bloodpike finds it strange that common soldiers were carrying the jeweled pendant Marg stole.",sec={{t="A Noble's Pendant",b="Nazeer Bloodpike finds it strange that common soldiers held a pendant like this. Its owner may have been in disguise, or the soldiers may have stolen it themselves. Either way, Nazeer judges it a noble's pendant, and its true owner must be found if the mystery is to unravel. Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar knows a great deal about Alliance politics, and can say whether the pendant belongs to Stormwind's nobility.",sp=0},{t="Zor's Verdict",b="Zor Lonetree admires the great skill that went into the pendant. Orcs would have no use for such a jewel, Zor says, but many humans would. Zor will have it studied and hopes that in time its mysteries will be revealed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the pendant being taken to Orgrimmar?",a="Nazeer Bloodpike judges it a noble's pendant. Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar knows a great deal about Alliance politics and can say whether it has a history among Stormwind's nobles.",al={"why send pendant to orgrimmar","why go to orgrimmar","why see zor lonetree"}},{q="Who previously had the jeweled pendant?",a="Marg stole it from soldiers of an Alliance camp near Theramore. Nazeer finds it strange that common soldiers held it, and wonders whether the owner was in disguise or the soldiers stole it.",al={"who had the pendant","where did the pendant come from"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="It follows Marg Speaks, where Marg told of stealing the pendant from soldiers camped near Theramore.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before"}},{q="Where is Zor Lonetree?",a="Zor Lonetree is in Orgrimmar.",al={"zor lonetree location","where is zor lonetree"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","jeweled pendant","marg speaks","nazeer bloodpike","orgrimmar","report to zor","stormwind","zor lonetree"},rel={"npc:zor-lonetree","quest:1261","quest:7541","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:orgrimmar","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance"},m={start="Nazeer Bloodpike",["end"]="Zor Lonetree",level="40",faction="Horde",id=1262},src={"Report to Zor"}}
E["quest:1268"] = {t="quest",n="Suspicious Hoofprints",z="dustwallow",s="Tracks of hooves stretch off from the Shady Rest Inn, whose bare frame still smokes. A few can be seen clearly, while more rows are nearly lost in the marsh's soft ground. Krog at Brackenwall Village is the one to report them to.",h="Tracks of hooves stretch off from the Shady Rest Inn, whose bare frame still smokes.",sec={{t="Prints in the Mud",b="The Shady Rest Inn is a bare frame now, still smoking, and trails of hoofprints stretch off from it. Some impressions are easy to see; others can hardly be made out in the soft ground. Krog at Brackenwall Village should hear about them.",sp=0},{t="Krog's Reply",b="Krog allows that the quilboar may have done it, or even the centaur, since both have a sizeable presence in the Barrens and the deed would not be hard to believe of them. Krog adds that the inn was not only burned: the inn's owner also lost a woman and a pup, both killed. Krog will send Kagoro to learn where the tracks lead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the hoofprints?",a="They lead away from the Shady Rest Inn, whose bare frame still smokes, over the marsh's soft ground.",al={"hoofprints location","where are tracks","shady rest inn prints"}},{q="Who should hear about the hoofprints?",a="Krog, at Brackenwall Village, is the one to report them to.",al={"who do I tell","krog location","where to report hoofprints"}},{q="How many prints are there?",a="A few are clearly visible, and further rows are nearly impossible to see in the mud.",al={"how many hoofprints","how many tracks"}}},kw={"brackenwall village","centaur","dustwallow marsh","hoofprints","kagoro","krog","quilboar","shady rest inn","suspicious hoofprints"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow","topic:centaur","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Hoofprints",["end"]="Krog",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1268},src={"Classic quest text: Suspicious Hoofprints"}}
E["quest:1269"] = {t="quest",n="Lieutenant Paval Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="Beneath the rubble lies a badge bearing Theramore's sign, a golden anchor over white enamel, with the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe embossed under the anchor. Krog at Brackenwall Village is the one to bring it to.",h="Beneath the rubble lies a badge bearing Theramore's sign, a golden anchor over white enamel, with the name...",sec={{t="A Glint in the Rubble",b="Something gleams beneath the rubble. Brushing off the ash and debris reveals a badge showing the sign of Theramore, with Lieutenant Paval Reethe's name embossed below it. Krog at Brackenwall Village awaits it, and will ask if you have a lead on what befell the Shady Rest Inn.",sp=0},{t="What Krog Knows",b="Krog knows this human, Paval Reethe, and calls him pathetic. By Krog's telling, Reethe abandoned the soldiers he served with and now hides out in the woods. Krog sent Ogron to track him down, since others suspect Reethe of stealing supplies. Krog thinks Ogron was seen going southeast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is on the badge?",a="The sign of Theramore, a golden anchor over white enamel, with the name Lieutenant Paval Reethe embossed beneath it.",al={"what does the badge say","theramore guard badge markings","who owns the badge"}},{q="Who gets the badge?",a="Krog, at Brackenwall Village, is who should see it.",al={"who do i bring the badge to","where does reethe's badge go","badge turn in"}},{q="Where was the badge found?",a="Beneath rubble, caked in ash and debris. Krog asks if you have a lead on what befell the Shady Rest Inn.",al={"badge location","where was reethes badge found"}}},kw={"badge","brackenwall","insignia","krog","ogron","paval","reethe","theramore"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Theramore Guard Badge",["end"]="Krog",level="37",faction="Horde",id=1269},src={"Classic quest text: Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}}
E["quest:1270"] = {t="quest",n="Stinky's Escape",z="dustwallow",s="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is hemmed in by swamp critters and has not found the bogbean he came for. Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin of Ratchet, wants bogbean leaves to brew a potion, and Ignatz asks you to get him out of this and watch over him while he searches. Afterward, Mebok Mizzyrix is to be found in Ratchet.",h="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is hemmed in by swamp critters and has not found the bogbean he came for.",sec={{t="Surrounded in the Swamp",b="Ignatz is relieved to meet someone who is not out to eat him. He says Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin from Ratchet, needs bogbean leaves to brew some potion or other. Ignatz claims not to care why, since the money was good and he knows this swamp. He got surrounded before finding the plant, and asks you to help him out of the spot and guard him while he looks for it.",sp=0},{t="Word From Mebok",b="Mebok says Ignatz came with the herbs and told how you got him out of trouble. A friend of Stinky's, Mebok declares, is a friend of Mebok's. Ignatz asked Mebok to hand you something if the two of you ever met, right before heading south to the marsh again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is \"Stinky\" Ignatz?",a="\"Stinky\" Ignatz is looking for bogbean leaves in the swamp for Mebok Mizzyrix. He says he knows the place, yet he got surrounded by critters before finding the plant.",al={"who is stinky","stinky ignatz","who is the escort guy"}},{q="Why is Ignatz gathering bogbean leaves?",a="The goblin Mebok Mizzyrix, from Ratchet, needs them for a potion. Ignatz says he does not care why, since the money was good.",al={"why bogbean","what is bogbean for","mebok bogbean"}},{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is a goblin from Ratchet who wants bogbean leaves to brew a potion.",al={"mebok","who is mebok mizzyrix","goblin in ratchet"}},{q="Who should you speak to afterward?",a="After seeing Ignatz through, find Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",al={"where does stinky go","where to turn in stinkys escape"}}},kw={"bogbean","dustwallow marsh","escort","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","stinky ignatz"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","subzone:ratchet","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="\"Stinky\" Ignatz",["end"]="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="37",faction="Horde",id=1270},src={"Classic quest text: Stinky's Escape"}}
E["quest:1271"] = {t="quest",n="Feast at the Blue Recluse",z="dustwallow",s="Your work for Morgan Stern in Dustwallow Marsh, ending with ... and Bugs, leads you back to Angus Stern at the Blue Recluse.",h="Your work for Morgan Stern in Dustwallow Marsh, ending with ...",sec={{t="Back to the Blue Recluse",b="Angus Stern is the uncle of Morgan Stern, whose recipe research you helped with in Dustwallow Marsh. Your road now leads back to Angus at the Blue Recluse.",sp=0},{t="What Angus Has Heard",b="Angus has heard from the nephew that you aided his research, and that you helped one of his associates out of a tight spot. The Sterns look after their own friends, and a party in your honor is about to begin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Angus Stern?",a="Angus Stern is the uncle of Morgan Stern, who gathers recipes in Theramore, and is connected to the Blue Recluse.",al={"angus stern","blue recluse host","who throws the feast"}},{q="How is Angus Stern connected to Morgan Stern?",a="Angus is Morgan's uncle. Angus sent Morgan to Theramore to gather recipes for the Blue Recluse's new bayou-themed menu.",al={"angus morgan relation","stern family","is morgan angus nephew"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows ... and Bugs, the last of the work you did for Morgan Stern in Theramore.",al={"previous quest","what comes before feast"}}},kw={"angus stern","dustwallow marsh","feast at the blue recluse","stern family","the blue recluse","morgan stern"},rel={"quest:1258","quest:1260","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Angus Stern",["end"]="Angus Stern",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1271},src={"Feast at the Blue Recluse"}}
E["quest:1273"] = {t="quest",n="Questioning Reethe",z="dustwallow",s="Ogron, whom Krog sent to track the human Reethe, has found him at last after a long search and says he hid well for a human. Ogron worries that so much time in the swamp may have driven Reethe mad, and asks you to come along to get answers from him. Afterward the way leads back to Krog at Brackenwall Village.",h="Ogron, whom Krog sent to track the human Reethe, has found him at last after a long search and says he hid...",sec={{t="Ogron's Search",b="After a long search, Ogron found Reethe, who by Ogron's reckoning hid well for a human. Ogron fears that so many days in the swamp may have left Reethe crazy, and wants you alongside to get answers from him. Afterward, Krog at Brackenwall Village awaits your return.",sp=0},{t="Back With Krog",b="Krog is pleased that Reethe is gone from the swamp, and scorns humans as built too frail to recover from even a small arrow wound. Krog concludes that this strand of the mystery led nowhere and that the search must look elsewhere.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who found Reethe?",a="Ogron found Reethe after a long search, and wants you along to get answers from him.",al={"who gives questioning reethe","questioning reethe quest giver","ogron reethe"}},{q="Why does Ogron want company?",a="Ogron worries that Reethe may have gone mad after so long in the swamp.",al={"why help ogron","is reethe crazy","why confront reethe"}},{q="Who do you report to afterward?",a="Krog, at Brackenwall Village.",al={"where to turn in questioning reethe","who do i talk to after reethe","reethe turn in"}}},kw={"brackenwall","dustwallow","interrogation","krog","marsh","ogron","reethe"},rel={"quest:1269","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Ogron",["end"]="Krog",level="37",id=1273},src={"Classic quest text: Questioning Reethe"}}
E["quest:1276"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Krog now recalls where the name Mosarn comes from: a highly regarded blacksmith in Thunder Bluff, whose armor set was once given to Krog by the Earthen Ring. Krog hopes Mosarn can say more about the blackened iron shield, since nothing useful came from Reethe. Mosarn is to be found in Thunder Bluff.",h="Krog now recalls where the name Mosarn comes from: a highly regarded blacksmith in Thunder Bluff, whose armor...",sec={{t="A Smith's Name",b="Krog remembers where the name Mosarn was heard before: a blacksmith in Thunder Bluff, highly regarded. The Earthen Ring once thanked Krog with armor that Mosarn crafted, and Krog speaks well of the work. Krog says Mosarn made the shield too and may be able to tell more about it. It is a slim lead, Krog admits, but Reethe yielded nothing useful, so it is all there is. The blackened iron shield goes to Mosarn, who is in Thunder Bluff.",sp=0},{t="Mosarn's Word",b="Mosarn agrees the shield is a piece of his own making, but can say little beyond that. He has made so many shields and armor sets that he cannot recall them all.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mosarn?",a="Mosarn is a highly regarded blacksmith in Thunder Bluff, who crafted an armor set the Earthen Ring gave to Krog.",al={"who is mosarn","where is mosarn","mosarn thunder bluff"}},{q="Why take the shield to Mosarn?",a="Krog says Mosarn made the shield and may be able to tell more about it. Krog calls it a weak lead, but with nothing useful learned from Reethe, it is all there is.",al={"why show mosarn the shield","blackened shield lead","what does mosarn know"}},{q="How does Krog know Mosarn?",a="The Earthen Ring gave Krog an armor set that Mosarn crafted, as thanks.",al={"krog mosarn connection","how does krog know the smith"}}},kw={"blackened iron shield","blacksmith","dustwallow","earthen ring","krog","mosarn","reethe","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:1323","zone:thunderbluff","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Krog",["end"]="Mosarn",level="37",id=1276},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1282"] = {t="quest",n="They Call Him Smiling Jim",z="dustwallow",s="Guard Byron feels sorry for a man called Smiling Jim and hints that he was not always the way he is now. Byron would rather not talk about it, and sends you to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",h="Guard Byron feels sorry for a man called Smiling Jim and hints that he was not always the way he is now.",sec={{t="A Sad Story",b="Byron pities Jim and says it was not always like this for him: Jim once kept an inn in the marsh, and a wonderful one. Byron prefers not to go into it. Anyone who truly wants the story is told to take it up with Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",sp=0},{t="Vimes's Account",b="Vimes names the man as James Hyal. Hyal set up an inn on the edge of the Barrens, meaning it as a pleasant stopover for travelers, and for a while it did well. Then Theramore lost its grip on the marsh roads, and the ogres moved in. Stubborn as he was, Hyal would not trade his dream for the safety of Theramore's walls, and fire consumed the Shady Rest Inn. Vimes says the investigation has had little luck so far, and suggests searching the rubble for anyone who wants to help.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Smiling Jim?",a="Guard Byron feels sorry for him and says he was not always like this. Byron remembers that Jim once kept an inn in the marsh, and a wonderful one.",al={"who is jim","smiling jim identity","who is the smiling man"}},{q="Why does Guard Byron send you to Captain Vimes?",a="Byron would rather not discuss Jim's past, and points you to Captain Garran Vimes instead.",al={"why talk to vimes","byron quest","guard byron reason"}},{q="Where do I find Captain Garran Vimes?",a="Captain Garran Vimes is in Theramore.",al={"who is captain vimes","captain vimes dustwallow"}}},kw={"captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","guard byron","james hyal","shady rest inn","smiling jim","theramore"},rel={"quest:1302","subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow","zone:barrens"},m={start="Guard Byron",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",id=1282},src={"Classic quest text: They Call Him Smiling Jim"}}
E["quest:1284"] = {t="quest",n="Suspicious Hoofprints",z="dustwallow",s="Hoofprints trail away from the smoking remains of the Shady Rest Inn. A few are easy to see, while others are nearly lost in the soft marsh mud. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore is the one to report them to.",h="Hoofprints trail away from the smoking remains of the Shady Rest Inn.",sec={{t="Prints in the Mud",b="Rows of prints run off from the Shady Rest Inn, whose ruin is still smoking. A handful of the impressions are plain to see, while further rows are all but invisible in the marsh's soft mud. Captain Garran Vimes, in Theramore, should hear of them.",sp=0},{t="What Vimes Makes of It",b="Vimes remarks that a great deal of centaur activity is found in the lands near Dustwallow Marsh. Short trips into the Barrens turned up their camps and holdings scattered across the area. Vimes will send Falgran Hastil, one of the trackers, to learn where the prints lead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the hoofprints found?",a="They trail away from the Shady Rest Inn, which is still smoking, across the soft marsh mud.",al={"where are the tracks","hoofprint location","shady rest inn prints"}},{q="Who receives the report about the prints?",a="Captain Garran Vimes, in Theramore.",al={"who do i tell about the hoofprints","who gets the hoofprints report","garran vimes hoofprints"}},{q="How easy are the prints to follow?",a="A few are clear, but many more rows are nearly invisible in the mud.",al={"are the prints hard to see","faint tracks marsh"}}},kw={"barrens","captain garran vimes","centaur","dustwallow marsh","falgran hastil","hoofprints","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","zone:dustwallow","topic:centaur","zone:barrens"},m={start="Hoofprints",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1284},src={"Classic quest text: Suspicious Hoofprints"}}
E["quest:1285"] = {t="quest",n="Daelin's Men",z="dustwallow",s="Adjutant Tesoran has found Lieutenant Paval Reethe in the guard's records. They tell of an enlistment in the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, distinguished service with promotions, and a place in the Theramore guard among the recruits who sailed over with Lady Proudmoore. The last entry lists Reethe as missing, and Captain Garran Vimes is to hear of it.",h="Adjutant Tesoran has found Lieutenant Paval Reethe in the guard's records.",sec={{t="What the Records Say",b="Captain Garran Vimes sent you to Adjutant Tesoran, who has now searched the books and found Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Reethe signed up with the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, and distinguished service brought promotions. Reethe went on to the Theramore guard, like most of the recruits who sailed over with Lady Proudmoore. The record ends with Reethe listed as missing. The news is for Vimes in Theramore.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Reaction",b="Vimes takes \"missing\" to be Tesoran's kind word for traitor. Vimes is sure Reethe is one of the fools whose loyalty to Admiral Daelin is blind enough to make them turn traitor, and finds a bitter irony in it, since the deserters accuse Theramore of betraying the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Adjutant Tesoran?",a="Adjutant Tesoran is the one who looked up Lieutenant Paval Reethe in the guard's records and read out what they say.",al={"tesoran","who gives daelins men"}},{q="What do the records say about Paval Reethe?",a="Reethe signed up with the Kul Tiras marines at sixteen, earned promotions through distinguished service, and later joined the Theramore guard among the recruits who sailed over with Lady Proudmoore. The record ends by listing Reethe as missing.",al={"reethe backstory","reethe record","paval reethe history"}},{q="Who gets the news about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes, in Theramore.",al={"why return to vimes","garran vimes reethe"}}},kw={"adjutant tesoran","daelin's men","deserters","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","kul tiras","paval reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1259","quest:1286","topic:kul-tiras","topic:alliance","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Adjutant Tesoran",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",id=1285},src={"Classic quest text: Daelin's Men"}}
E["quest:1286"] = {t="quest",n="The Deserters",z="dustwallow",s="Captain Garran Vimes says deserters have settled into a tower that Theramore had abandoned. The tower stands at Lost Point, which lies southeast of the inn. A man called Jacken leads the deserters, and Vimes wants information about Reethe from him.",h="Captain Garran Vimes says deserters have settled into a tower that Theramore had abandoned.",sec={{t="A Tower Taken",b="Vimes admits that holding on in the marsh has been a struggle, though the resolve of Vimes's people has kept several defensive watchtowers standing. Scouting reports say deserters have moved into an abandoned one at Lost Point, which lies southeast of the inn. A man named Jacken leads them. Vimes asks you to see what information Jacken will give up about Reethe, and warns that Jacken may not part with it easily.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to deal with the deserters?",a="Captain Garran Vimes, whose scouting reports say deserters have settled into one of the towers Theramore abandoned.",al={"who starts the deserters","who gives the deserters quest"}},{q="Where are the deserters hiding?",a="At Lost Point, which lies southeast of the inn, in an abandoned tower in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"deserters location","where is lost point"}},{q="Who leads the deserters at Lost Point?",a="A man called Jacken, or Balos Jacken, leads them. Vimes warns that Jacken may not give up information easily.",al={"who is balos jacken","deserter leader"}},{q="What does Captain Vimes want from Balos Jacken?",a="Information about Reethe, from Jacken and the deserters.",al={"why find jacken","what does vimes want"}}},kw={"balos jacken","captain garran vimes","deserters","dustwallow marsh","lost point","reethe","watchtower"},rel={"quest:1285","quest:1287","subzone:lost-point","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Balos Jacken",level="38",id=1286},src={"Classic quest text: The Deserters"}}
E["quest:1287"] = {t="quest",n="The Deserters",z="dustwallow",s="Asked about Reethe, Balos Jacken, leader of the Lost Point deserters, calls him a coward and says the deserters drove him from their camp. Jacken then asks you to forget you ever ran into them. Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore is the one to tell about Reethe.",h="Asked about Reethe, Balos Jacken, leader of the Lost Point deserters, calls him a coward and says the...",sec={{t="Thrown Out",b="Jacken says the deserters drove Reethe out for repeatedly plundering the ogres' stores at Brackenwall Village. By Jacken's account the deserters are too few to stand against those ogres, and Reethe crossed the line once too often, so the band left him to manage alone. In return for the answer, Jacken asks that you forget the meeting.",sp=0},{t="Back in Theramore",b="Vimes says Lieutenant Caldwell will be sent against the Lost Point deserters, and will be told to find Reethe as well. Vimes judges the marsh neither large nor trackless enough to keep Caldwell from finding Reethe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Reethe thrown out of the deserter camp?",a="Jacken says Reethe kept plundering the ogres' stores at Brackenwall Village. The deserters are too few to stand against them, so they left Reethe to manage alone.",al={"why did deserters exile reethe","reethe brackenwall village","why did balos kick out reethe"}},{q="Who is Balos Jacken?",a="Jacken leads the Lost Point deserters. Asked about Reethe, he calls him a coward.",al={"who is balos jacken","balos jacken lore","balos jacken dustwallow"}},{q="Who wants to hear about Reethe?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore, though Jacken himself hopes you will forget you ever met the deserters.",al={"where to turn in the deserters","who wants reethe information"}}},kw={"balos jacken","brackenwall village","caldwell","deserters","garran vimes","lost point","reethe","theramore"},rel={"quest:1286","subzone:lost-point","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Balos Jacken",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",id=1287},src={"Classic quest text: The Deserters"}}
E["quest:1288"] = {t="quest",n="Vimes's Report",z="dustwallow",s="Captain Garran Vimes rates your work as the best Vimes has seen from an amateur. Lady Jaina Proudmoore asked Vimes to keep her apprised of a delicate situation, and Vimes gives you the report to bring to her in Theramore.",h="Captain Garran Vimes rates your work as the best Vimes has seen from an amateur.",sec={{t="A Report for Lady Proudmoore",b="Lady Proudmoore asked Captain Vimes to keep her apprised of a delicate situation, and Vimes has not spoken with her for some time. Vimes meant to deliver the report later, but now judges it more fitting for you to speak with her about it, since you may well have better answers for her questions than Vimes would.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives you the report to take to Jaina Proudmoore?",a="Captain Garran Vimes hands you Vimes's report to carry to Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore.",al={"who starts vimes's report","who gives the report","who wrote vimes report"}},{q="Why does Captain Vimes send you instead of going himself?",a="Vimes has not spoken with Lady Proudmoore for some time, and thinks it more fitting that you go instead. Vimes believes you may have better answers for her questions.",al={"why send me","why not vimes deliver it","why jaina report"}},{q="Where does the report need to go?",a="To Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore.",al={"where to turn in vimes report","where is jaina proudmoore","report destination"}}},kw={"dustwallow","garran vimes","jaina proudmoore","report","theramore","vimes"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Lady Jaina Proudmoore",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1288},src={"Wowpedia: Vimes's Report"}}
E["quest:1289"] = {t="quest",n="Vimes's Report",z="dustwallow",s="Lady Jaina Proudmoore has read Captain Garran Vimes's report and thanks you for your help with the investigation. She asks you to return to Vimes and help get to the bottom of the mystery.",h="Lady Jaina Proudmoore has read Captain Garran Vimes's report and thanks you for your help with the...",sec={{t="Back to the Captain",b="Going by Captain Vimes's report, Lady Proudmoore sees that you have been a great help to his investigation, and she thanks you for it. She is easier in her mind knowing the matter rests in such capable hands. She asks you to return to Captain Vimes in Theramore and help him get to the bottom of this mystery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you back to Captain Vimes?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore, once she has read Vimes's report in Theramore.",al={"who gives vimes report","jaina quest giver","who sends me to vimes"}},{q="What does Lady Jaina think of the report?",a="She says you have been a great help to the investigation and thanks you for it. Knowing the matter is in capable hands lets her rest easier.",al={"jaina reaction","what does jaina say about vimes report"}},{q="Where do you find Captain Garran Vimes?",a="Captain Garran Vimes is in Theramore.",al={"where is captain vimes","captain vimes location","where to turn in vimes report"}}},kw={"captain garran vimes","dustwallow marsh","investigation","lady jaina proudmoore","theramore","vimes's report"},rel={"quest:1288","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Lady Jaina Proudmoore",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=1289},src={"Wowpedia: Vimes's Report (2)"}}
E["quest:1319"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Captain Garran Vimes is sorry to be of little help with the Blackened Iron Shield, but knows who can do better: Caz Twosprocket, one of the best blacksmiths around, who tends the forge in Theramore's smithy.",h="Captain Garran Vimes is sorry to be of little help with the Blackened Iron Shield, but knows who can do...",sec={{t="A Smith Who Can Say",b="Vimes apologizes for being unable to help much with the shield, but names someone who can. You are sent with it to Caz Twosprocket, one of the best blacksmiths, who tends the forge in Theramore's smithy. Perhaps Caz can tell you something about it.",sp=0},{t="The Smith's Opinion",b="Caz looks the iron over and calls it an interesting piece. It is not Caz's own work, and certainly not the work of any smith Caz knows of this side of the water.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to examine the shield?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore, who is sorry to be of little help with it and points you to someone better.",al={"who gives the black shield","black shield quest starter","who starts the black shield"}},{q="Who is Caz Twosprocket?",a="A blacksmith who tends the forge in Theramore's smithy. Vimes counts him among the best.",al={"caz twosprocket","who is the blacksmith in theramore"}},{q="What shield is shown to Caz?",a="The Blackened Iron Shield.",al={"blackened iron shield","what shield do i show caz"}}},kw={"blackened iron shield","captain garran vimes","caz twosprocket","dustwallow marsh","the black shield","theramore"},rel={"quest:1253","quest:1320","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Captain Garran Vimes",["end"]="Caz Twosprocket",level="35",id=1319},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1320"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Caz Twosprocket studies the black shield tied to the Shady Rest Inn mystery. One detail nearly escapes notice, and Caz sends you to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore with what was found.",h="Caz Twosprocket studies the black shield tied to the Shady Rest Inn mystery.",sec={{t="A Strap Burned Away",b="A last detail nearly escapes Caz Twosprocket while looking over the black shield. The leather strap on its back has burned away, yet it seems to have been made for a large person. Caz guesses a tauren. That is all Caz can tell, so you are sent to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore with the word and Caz's apology for not being more help.",sp=0},{t="What Vimes Makes of It",b="Captain Garran Vimes finds little to go on in what Caz has learned. Still, he says he will keep it in mind. He hopes other pieces of the mystery will fall into place and show more clearly what happened.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Caz Twosprocket find out about the shield?",a="The leather strap on the shield's back has burned away, but it seems to have been made for a large person. Caz guesses a tauren.",al={"caz findings","shield clues","black shield clue"}},{q="Who should hear what Caz found?",a="Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.",al={"who do i tell about the shield","turn in black shield","where to report shield"}}},kw={"black shield","caz twosprocket","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","shady rest inn","tauren","theramore"},rel={"subzone:shady-rest-inn","topic:tauren","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Caz Twosprocket",["end"]="Captain Garran Vimes",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1320},src={"The Black Shield (Alliance 3)"}}
E["quest:1321"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Krog looks over the Blackened Iron Shield and sees nothing unusual about it. Krog suggests that the blacksmith Do'gol inspect it, though without much hope, and sends you to Brackenwall Village.",h="Krog looks over the Blackened Iron Shield and sees nothing unusual about it.",sec={{t="A Second Opinion",b="Krog sees nothing unusual about the shield. Do'gol, the blacksmith, might be able to tell more about it, Krog says, but warns against expecting much. Do'gol is in Brackenwall Village.",sp=0},{t="Do'gol's Answer",b="Do'gol calls it a good shield, strong and heavy. Do'gol has no need of it, though, being a maker of shields and not a buyer, and says you should know that.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Do'gol with the shield?",a="Krog, who looked over the Blackened Iron Shield and found nothing unusual about it.",al={"who gives the black shield quest","where do i start the black shield","black shield questgiver"}},{q="Where can Do'gol be found?",a="Do'gol is the blacksmith in Brackenwall Village.",al={"dogol location","where is dogol","find dogol"}},{q="Why does Krog send you to Do'gol?",a="Krog hopes the blacksmith can tell more about the shield, though Krog does not expect much to come of it.",al={"why visit dogol","why show the shield to the blacksmith"}}},kw={"black shield","blackened iron shield","brackenwall village","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","krog"},rel={"quest:1251","quest:1322","subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Krog",["end"]="Do'gol",level="35",id=1321},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1322"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="At Brackenwall Village, Do'gol has noticed lettering along the shield's edge, but burned residue hides it. Clearing it needs acid, and Do'gol asks you for six venom sacs from the Darkfang spiders of the marsh.",h="At Brackenwall Village, Do'gol has noticed lettering along the shield's edge, but burned residue hides it.",sec={{t="Cleaning the Rim",b="Do'gol can see lettering around the shield's rim, though the burnt-on grime makes it hard to read. Acid would clear it, and the marsh's Darkfang spiders carry venom that works well. Do'gol wants six of their acidic venom sacs to clean the shield up.",sp=0},{t="Once the Sacs Arrive",b="Do'gol takes a dislike to spiders too large to sit on and squash, then thanks you for the sacs. Do'gol rips them open and pours them onto the shield.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the spider venom?",a="Do'gol, in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who gives the black shield","dogol quest","who starts the black shield"}},{q="Why does Do'gol need venom sacs?",a="Do'gol wants acid to clear the burned residue hiding the writing on the shield's rim, and Darkfang spider venom will do.",al={"why spider acid","purpose of acidic venom sacs","why clean the shield"}},{q="Where do the acidic venom sacs come from?",a="From the Darkfang spiders that live in the marsh near Brackenwall Village.",al={"which spiders have sacs","darkfang spider location","where to get acidic venom"}},{q="How many sacs does Do'gol want?",a="Six Acidic Venom Sacs.",al={"how many venom sacs"}}},kw={"acidic venom sacs","brackenwall village","darkfang","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","the black shield"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Do'gol",["end"]="Do'gol",level="37",id=1322},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:1323"] = {t="quest",n="The Black Shield",z="dustwallow",s="Do'gol has rubbed the shield clear enough to see what appears to spell Mosarn, a name that means nothing to Do'gol. Krog in Brackenwall Village knows many people, so Do'gol sends you to ask there.",h="Do'gol has rubbed the shield clear enough to see what appears to spell Mosarn, a name that means nothing to...",sec={{t="A Name on the Rim",b="Do'gol poured on a bit too much acid, but a little rubbing brings out writing that is still hard to read and seems to say Mosarn. The name means nothing to Do'gol. Krog in Brackenwall Village knows many people, so Do'gol sends you to talk with Krog.",sp=0},{t="Krog's Answer",b="Krog finds the name Mosarn familiar but cannot place it, and hopes it will come back later. Krog adds that it probably does not matter, since shields turn up from all sorts of places and carry no meaning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Do'gol?",a="The one in Brackenwall Village who has been cleaning the shield with acid to read its writing.",al={"dogol","who gives the black shield"}},{q="What name is on the shield?",a="Do'gol thinks the writing spells Mosarn, though it is hard to read, and has never heard of anyone by that name.",al={"what name is on the shield","who is mosarn","shield inscription name"}},{q="Why talk to Krog about the shield?",a="Do'gol does not know who Mosarn is, but says Krog knows many people.",al={"why talk to krog","who is krog"}},{q="Where is Krog located?",a="Krog is in Brackenwall Village.",al={"krog location","where do i find krog"}}},kw={"acid","black shield","brackenwall village","do'gol","dustwallow marsh","krog","mosarn"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Do'gol",["end"]="Krog",level="37",id=1323},src={"Classic quest text: The Black Shield"}}
E["quest:7541"] = {t="quest",n="Service to the Horde",z="dustwallow",s="The jeweled pendant now sits with Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar, delivered after Report to Zor, and Zor has one more word for you.",h="The jeweled pendant now sits with Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar, delivered after Report to Zor, and Zor has one...",sec={{t="Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar",b="You carried the jeweled pendant to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar, and the pendant now sits with Zor. Return to Zor Lonetree and there is more to hear about what you have done for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Zor's Last Word",b="Zor says the scholars will need time to study the pendant. For your service to the Horde, Zor offers a small token, and says that what you have done brings honor to you and to the Horde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who has the pendant now?",a="Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar, after you carried it there from Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.",al={"who takes the pendant","who gives this quest","zor lonetree role"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Report to Zor, where you took the jeweled pendant to Zor Lonetree.",al={"what quest came before","service to the horde prerequisite","previous quest"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","pendant","report to zor","service to the horde","zor lonetree"},rel={"npc:zor-lonetree","quest:1262","topic:horde","zone:dustwallow"},m={start="Zor Lonetree",["end"]="Zor Lonetree",level="40",faction="Horde",id=7541},src={"Service to the Horde"}}
E["subzone:beezil-s-wreck"] = {t="subzone",n="Beezil's Wreck",z="dustwallow",s="Beezil's Wreck marks the crash site of an unfortunate goblin zeppelin deep within the quagmires of Dustwallow Marsh. Resting east of Tabetha's Farm, the shattered vessel's cargo holds scattered supplies and volatile engineering components that attract scavengers.",h="Beezil's Wreck marks the crash site of an unfortunate goblin zeppelin deep within the quagmires of Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Calamitous Landing",b="Hidden away in the humid muck east of Tabetha's Farm lies the splintered skeleton of a goblin zeppelin known as Beezil's Wreck. The craft was hauling cargo southward across Kalimdor before suffering a disastrous plunge into the swamp. While the wreckage still smolders amid tangled reeds, its eccentric captain, Beezil, has seemingly vanished from the marsh, leaving behind scattered crates and ticking machinery to slowly rot in the brine.",sp=0},{t="Salvage in the Muck",b="Despite the harsh environment, the crash site remains a prime target for opportunistic explorers. The airship carried a payload of volatile goods, notably Seaforium boosters and heavy crates that survived the impact. Scavengers daring enough to wade through the surrounding beasts often risk life and limb to secure what is left of the lost shipment before corrosive marsh water ruins the haul entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beezil's Wreck?",a="Beezil's Wreck is the crash site of a goblin zeppelin situated deep in Dustwallow Marsh, directly east of Tabetha's Farm. The airship came down while transporting cargo across the marsh.",al={"beezils wreck","crashed zeppelin dustwallow","what is this wreck"}},{q="Where is the pilot, Beezil?",a="The pilot, Beezil, is nowhere to be found around the crash site. Whether he escaped into the treacherous wilderness or fled the marsh entirely remains a mystery to those searching the hull.",al={"where is beezil","who is beezil","beezil location"}},{q="What valuable cargo was the zeppelin carrying?",a="The zeppelin was loaded with trade goods and volatile goblin technology, including Seaforium boosters. These valuable engineering components make the site a frequent target for adventurers and salvagers.",al={"what was in the zeppelin","seaforium boosters","wreck cargo"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The twisted wreckage of a goblin zeppelin holds volatile mechanical components, particularly Seaforium boosters that any tinkerer would covet.",["race:Gnome"]="Examining the smoking remains of rival goblin aviation offers a morbid reminder of the perils inherent in non-gnomish aerial design."},kw={"beezil","beezil's wreck","dustwallow marsh","seaforium","tabetha","zeppelin crash"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","npc:tabetha","topic:goblin"},src={"Beezil's Wreck"}}
E["subzone:bloodfen-burrow"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodfen Burrow",z="dustwallow",s="Bloodfen Burrow is a cavern in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with vicious raptors. The beasts have claimed the cave and the surrounding clearing, completely overrunning the ruins of a settlement that once tried to survive the wetlands.",h="Bloodfen Burrow is a cavern in southwestern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with vicious raptors.",sec={{t="A Den of Predators",b="Tucked away in the southwestern reaches of Dustwallow Marsh, Bloodfen Burrow serves as the primary den for the region's aggressive Bloodfen raptors. The cave mouth and surrounding hollow crawl with the pack, drawn to the sheltered crevice and the bountiful hunting ground the marsh provides. Just outside the entrance lie scattered debris and splintered remains of an unidentified settlement, serving as a grim reminder of who truly rules the swamp's interior. Travelers also whisper that Cortello, an adventurous buccaneer, left one of his hidden riddle clues somewhere within this deadly den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What lives in Bloodfen Burrow?",a="The burrow is overrun by Bloodfen raptors. They have established a dense nesting ground both inside the cave and across the surrounding clearing, attacking anyone foolish enough to intrude on their territory.",al={"who lives here","bloodfen burrow raptors","what mobs in bloodfen burrow"}},{q="What are the ruins outside the cave?",a="The remains of an unidentified settlement lie outside the cave. Raptors destroyed the settlement, but the identity and fate of its occupants are not recorded.",al={"ruined settlement dustwallow","who built the huts near bloodfen burrow","ruins outside cave"}},{q="Why would an adventurer search Bloodfen Burrow?",a="Aside from hunting the fierce marsh raptors, explorers deciphering Cortello's Riddle must venture inside the burrow. The pirate left one of his riddle clues concealed within the cavern's shadowy depths.",al={"cortello's riddle bloodfen","treasure in bloodfen burrow","bloodfen burrow quest"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The Bloodfen raptors nesting here are fierce, quick beasts well-suited for hunters seeking durable, aggressive swamp companions."},kw={"bloodfen burrow","bloodfen raptor","cortello's riddle","dustwallow marsh","raptor cave"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Bloodfen Burrow"}}
E["subzone:bluefen"] = {t="subzone",n="Bluefen",z="dustwallow",s="Bluefen is a soggy marshland nestled in northern Dustwallow Marsh just east of Brackenwall Village. Crawling with aggressive wetland predators, the mire has also become a staging ground for covert Theramore Infiltrators keeping watch on local Horde movements.",h="Bluefen is a soggy marshland nestled in northern Dustwallow Marsh just east of Brackenwall Village.",sec={{t="A Contested Bog",b="Situated just east of the Stonemaul ogres of Brackenwall Village, Bluefen embodies the untamed hazards of Dustwallow Marsh. The humid swampland teems with predatory beasts, including raptors, giant spiders, carrion-feeding birds, and lurking crocolisks. Beyond natural predators, travelers must contend with Theramore Infiltrators who skulk through the murky terrain to spy on the Horde and project human influence deeper into the swamp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bluefen located?",a="Bluefen lies in northern Dustwallow Marsh, situated just east of Brackenwall Village.",al={"bluefen location","where is bluefen","bluefen map"}},{q="What threats can be found in Bluefen?",a="The marsh is infested with dangerous wildlife including spiders, crocolisks, raptors, and marsh birds. Additionally, covert Theramore Infiltrators scout the area, posing a threat to Horde travelers.",al={"bluefen enemies","what lives in bluefen","bluefen mobs"}},{q="Why are Theramore scouts active in Bluefen?",a="Theramore Infiltrators monitor northern Dustwallow Marsh from Bluefen, watching the neighboring Stonemaul ogre settlement of Brackenwall Village and patrolling the contested pathways of the marsh.",al={"theramore infiltrators","why are alliance here","theramore spies"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just east of Brackenwall Village, Bluefen poses a double danger to Horde champions: fierce swamp beasts and watchful Theramore Infiltrators spying on your Stonemaul allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="While wild beasts make travel treacherous, Theramore scouts use the dense marshland foliage of Bluefen to keep watchful eyes on the nearby ogre encampment."},kw={"bluefen","brackenwall","crocolisks","dustwallow","marsh","theramore infiltrators"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village"},src={"Bluefen"}}
E["subzone:brackenwall-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Brackenwall Village",z="dustwallow",s="Brackenwall Village is the primary Horde outpost in Dustwallow Marsh, nestled among the bogs in the northwest corner of the zone. Founded by surviving Stonemaul ogres after dragons devastated their original settlement to the south, the village serves as a tenuous stronghold surrounded by Alliance spies, deserters, and the black dragonflight.",h="Brackenwall Village is the primary Horde outpost in Dustwallow Marsh, nestled among the bogs in the northwest...",sec={{t="Refuge of the Stonemaul",b="When black dragonkin drove the Stonemaul ogres out of their ancient home at Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh, their leader, Overlord Mok'Morokk—successor to Rexxar—led the survivors north into the swamp to build Brackenwall. Formed around traditional earthen mounds, huts, and an old watchtower, the settlement gave the battered clan a defensible haven. Though aligned with the Horde, the village suffers from internal rot: Mok'Morokk sits idle, hoarding supplies and refusing to confront the draconic threat, leaving the clan's spiritual and tactical guidance to figures like the ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde emissaries.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Bog",b="Beyond internal dysfunction, Brackenwall is beset by external threats. Theramore infiltrators lurk constantly in the thickets, spying on village movements and reporting back to the island fortress. Meanwhile, Paval Reethe, a Theramore deserter cast out from Lost Point, is suspected of stealing vital supplies from the outpost. Between wary eyes watching from the east and black drakes prowling the southern reaches, Brackenwall serves as the Horde's isolated staging ground to keep both the Alliance and Onyxia's brood at bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there ogres allied with the Horde here?",a="These are the Stonemaul ogres, an honorable clan inducted into the modern Horde by the champion Rexxar during the founding of Durotar. Rexxar became their chieftain after defeating their former leader, binding the clan to Warchief Thrall's new coalition before passing leadership to Mok'Morokk.",al={"why horde ogres","stonemaul clan lore","who are these ogres"}},{q="Why did the Stonemaul settle here instead of staying in their old home?",a="Their ancestral settlement in southern Dustwallow Marsh was overrun and obliterated by the black dragonflight. Overlord Mok'Morokk led the displaced survivors northward into the bog to establish Brackenwall as a fortified refuge.",al={"what happened to stonemaul village","why brackenwall","ogre refugees"}},{q="Who is in charge of Brackenwall Village?",a="Overlord Mok'Morokk leads the settlement, though his reign is widely resented. Rather than rallying his people to retake their homeland or confront the dragons, he cowers inside the village, forcing the ogre mage Draz'Zilb and Horde envoys to manage daily crises.",al={"brackenwall leader","who runs brackenwall","mok'morokk"}},{q="Why are there Theramore spies outside the village?",a="Despite the fragile truce between Theramore and Orgrimmar, Lady Jaina Proudmoore's military keeps close surveillance on any Horde troop movements within Dustwallow. Infiltrators skirt the perimeter of Brackenwall, reporting on ogre strength and Horde operations.",al={"alliance spies dustwallow","theramore infiltrators","why is theramore watching"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Brackenwall is your sole sanctuary and flight connection in the marsh; defending it ensures the Horde maintains a vital listening post and defensive flank against Theramore.",["faction:Alliance"]="Brackenwall is deep in hostile territory, but investigations concerning the missing diplomat and rogue Theramore deserters will bring daring agents right to the edge of the ogre encampment."},kw={"brackenwall","draz'zilb","dustwallow","infiltrators","mok'morokk","ogres","paval reethe","stonemaul"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","topic:horde","npc:onyxia","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:lost-point","quest:1241"},src={"Brackenwall Village"}}
E["subzone:darkmist-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkmist Cavern",z="dustwallow",s="Darkmist Cavern is an abandoned mine tucked into northwestern Dustwallow Marsh, completely infested with predatory giant spiders. Crumbling ruins outside hint at an unfortunate former settlement swallowed up by the marsh's hazards. Locals remain divided on whether the cavern gave its name to the arachnids or the reverse.",h="Darkmist Cavern is an abandoned mine tucked into northwestern Dustwallow Marsh, completely infested with...",sec={{t="The Brood in the Mine",b="Situated in the northwest reaches of Dustwallow Marsh, Darkmist Cavern appears to have once been an active mining venture. Today, any human presence has long vanished, leaving behind rotting, ruined shacks outside the entrance and a network of tunnels choked with thick webs. The cavern is overrun by Darkmist spiders, predatory horrors whose venom and size make the tunnels deadly to unwary wanderers. Marsh dwellers still dispute whether the cavern was named after the foul brood nesting inside or if the spiders took the title from the misty cave itself.",sp=0},{t="Hermit's Larder",b="Despite the obvious danger, the cavern attracts occasional scavengers and eccentric marshfolk. The hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl is notorious for sending travelers deep into the webs to harvest the eyes of these monstrous spiders, insisting they make a fine stock for broth. Aside from such eccentric culinary outings, most sensible travelers steer well clear of the web-strewn entrance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Darkmist Cavern?",a="It is an abandoned mine in northwestern Dustwallow Marsh that has fallen entirely into the possession of giant, venomous spiders known as Darkmist spiders.",al={"what is darkmist cavern","darkmist cave","spider cave dustwallow"}},{q="Who lived at the ruins outside the cave?",a="The small wooden ruins suggest a settlement or mining camp once operated here, but its former inhabitants are not identified.",al={"who lived here","houses outside darkmist cavern","abandoned village darkmist"}},{q="Why do locals venture into Darkmist Cavern?",a="Very few willingly enter, but the eccentric hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl hires daring adventurers to dive into the tunnels and retrieve spider eyes to brew into his strange marsh stew.",al={"why go to darkmist cavern","darkmist cavern quest"}},{q="Did the spiders or the cavern get the name first?",a="The inhabitants of Dustwallow Marsh disagree on whether the spiders were named after the cavern or the cavern after the spiders. No settled account establishes which name came first.",al={"spider name origin","why is it called darkmist"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The eccentric hermit 'Swamp Eye' Jarl considers the foul eyes of Darkmist spiders to be the prime ingredient for a hearty marsh stew, though few outside the swamp share his taste.",["profession:Mining"]="The cavern was clearly hollowed out by past miners, but anyone looking to prospect its rocky depths will have to fight through hordes of nesting spiders first."},kw={"darkmist cavern","darkmist spiders","dustwallow marsh","mine ruins","spider mine","swamp eye jarl"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Darkmist Cavern"}}
E["subzone:den-of-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Den of Flame",z="dustwallow",s="The Den of Flame is a fortified cavern in western Dustwallow Marsh, situated just west of the Stonemaul Ruins. Originally constructed by the Stonemaul ogres as their mound, it has since been overrun by the dragonkin of the black dragonflight serving Onyxia.",h="The Den of Flame is a fortified cavern in western Dustwallow Marsh, situated just west of the Stonemaul Ruins.",sec={{t="A Conquered Mound",b="Built by the Stonemaul ogres to serve as their main mound and sanctuary, the Den of Flame bears the unmistakable, rough-hewn stone architecture of ogre masonry. However, when the black dragonflight laid waste to the Stonemaul clan's settlement, the brood did not merely scatter the ogres—they seized the stronghold for themselves. Today, black dragonspawn patrol the burning perimeter and cavern entrance under the shadow of Onyxia's nearby lair.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Den of Flame originally built for?",a="The structure was originally built by the Stonemaul ogres to serve as their clan's primary mound. Its stonework and layout mirror classic ogre clan architecture.",al={"who built den of flame","den of flame origin","ogre mound dustwallow"}},{q="Why are black dragonkin infesting this mound?",a="The great black dragon Onyxia established her lair in the marsh nearby. Her dragonkin drove the Stonemaul ogres out of their settlement and claimed the cavern as a forward outpost for the brood.",al={"why are there dragons here","who lives in den of flame","dragonspawn dustwallow"}},{q="Can the Stonemaul ogres reclaim the cave?",a="Not for now. The surviving Stonemaul ogres have settled at Brackenwall Village alongside the Horde, while the black dragonspawn hold their old mound in force.",al={"reclaiming the den"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are sworn allies of the Horde; clearing out the dragonkin in the Den of Flame helps avenge their fallen settlement."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul ruins"},rel={"subzone:stonemaul-ruins","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Den of Flame"}}
E["subzone:dragonmurk"] = {t="subzone",n="Dragonmurk",z="dustwallow",s="Dragonmurk is a sprawling, hazardous tract of southern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with black dragonspawn and hatchlings. Flanked by ancient ogre ruins and scorched caverns, it serves as the hostile outer perimeter for the brood of Onyxia.",h="Dragonmurk is a sprawling, hazardous tract of southern Dustwallow Marsh swarming with black dragonspawn and...",sec={{t="A Brood in the Bog",b="Spanning the southern interior of Dustwallow Marsh, the Dragonmurk marks the threshold where damp wetlands give way to the dominion of the black dragonflight. The waterways and thick mud here crawl with black wyrmkins, dragonspawn, and ravenous whelps. The surrounding landscape has suffered deeply from their presence; adjacent territories such as the ruined village of Stonemaul and the scorched cavern known as the Den of Flame have both fallen completely under the flight's territorial grip.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Broodmother",b="The swarms of drakes and guards throughout the Dragonmurk are not random wanderers. Southern Dustwallow serves as the primary nesting ground in Kalimdor for Onyxia, the daughter of Deathwing. The wyrmkin patrol the mire aggressively, annihilating interlopers and protecting the clutch from both Theramore's scouts and the Horde's nearby encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dragonmurk?",a="Dragonmurk is the southern region of Dustwallow Marsh that is heavily infested with whelps, drakes, and dragonspawn belonging to the black dragonflight.",al={"what is dragonmurk","where is dragonmurk","dragonmurk location"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons here?",a="Southern Dustwallow Marsh contains the lair of Onyxia, a broodmother of the black dragonflight. Dragonmurk acts as a protective buffer where her offspring and servants can nest, mature, and ward off outside threats.",al={"why black dragons in dustwallow","who leads the dragons here","onyxia dragons dustwallow"}},{q="What landmarks are found near Dragonmurk?",a="Dragonmurk encompasses and surrounds key sites including the Den of Flame and the Stonemaul Ruins, both of which have been overrun and occupied by black dragonspawn.",al={"dragonmurk landmarks","what is near dragonmurk","places around dragonmurk"}},{q="Is Dragonmurk safe for travelers?",a="Not at all. The dragonkin in Dragonmurk are uniformly hostile and aggressive, making it one of the most perilous wilderness regions in southern Kalimdor.",al={"is dragonmurk dangerous","can i walk through dragonmurk"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The dragons in Dragonmurk drove the Stonemaul ogres from their village and continually endanger Horde expeditions venturing deep into the marsh.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore keeps a wary eye on the Dragonmurk, knowing that an unchecked black dragon brood so close to the fortress could easily spell disaster."},kw={"black dragonflight","den of flame","dragonmurk","dragonspawn","dustwallow marsh","onyxia","stonemaul ruins","whelps"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:den-of-flame","subzone:stonemaul-ruins"},src={"Dragonmurk"}}
E["subzone:dreadmurk-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmurk Shore",z="dustwallow",s="Dreadmurk Shore encompasses the foggy coastline and scattered islands of Dustwallow Marsh running north toward the Barrens. Dominated by aggressive Mirefin murlocs and sea beasts, these treacherous waters have recently become the hiding ground for shipwrecked Defias Brotherhood outlaws.",h="Dreadmurk Shore encompasses the foggy coastline and scattered islands of Dustwallow Marsh running north...",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coast",b="Stretching along the northeastern edge of Dustwallow Marsh between Theramore Isle and Northwatch Hold, Dreadmurk Shore is a dismal expanse of muddy shoals, tide pools, and misty islands. The coast is overrun by the Mirefin tribe, a territorial clan of murlocs that aggressively attacks any travelers nearing their coastal villages. Sea turtles and aquatic predators prowl the shallows, making the shoreline dangerous to navigate even without factoring in the surrounding swamplands.",sp=0},{t="Defias Infiltrators",b="Beyond the indigenous swamp creatures, the shoreline has drawn heightened scrutiny from Theramore due to the presence of human outlaws. A ship bearing the Defias Brotherhood met disaster in the waters between the shore and Alcaz Island, spilling brigands onto the sand and islets. The presence of these Eastern Kingdoms criminals so close to Lady Jaina Proudmoore's stronghold is an alarming development that threatens the fragile balance of power across the bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Dreadmurk Shore located?",a="Dreadmurk Shore stretches along the northeastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, facing the Great Sea between the outskirts of Theramore Isle and the border of the Barrens near Northwatch Hold.",al={"dreadmurk shore location","where is dreadmurk shore"}},{q="Why are there Defias bandits on this shore?",a="A Defias Brotherhood vessel recently wrecked in the waters offshore between Dreadmurk and Alcaz Island. The survivors scrambled ashore, establishing temporary camps along the isolated beach and outcroppings while trying to salvage their sunken cargo.",al={"defias in dustwallow","why are defias here","shipwrecked defias"}},{q="Who are the murlocs living along the beach?",a="The coast is heavily populated by the Mirefin murloc tribe. They have built crude fishing settlements along the sandbanks and rocky islets, fiercely guarding their territory from both Theramore patrols and shipwrecked intruders.",al={"mirefin murlocs","dreadmurk shore murlocs"}},{q="Is Dreadmurk Shore controlled by Theramore?",a="Theramore claims nominal authority over the lands surrounding the island, but Dreadmurk Shore is functionally lawless. Its marshy shoals are too wild and infested with murlocs and brigands for Lady Jaina Proudmoore's sentries to maintain regular patrols.",al={"who owns dreadmurk shore","is dreadmurk shore alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The discovery of Defias Brotherhood survivors so close to Theramore suggests conspiracies that reach far beyond Westfall, directly threatening Alliance stability in Kalimdor.",["class:Rogue"]="The isolated camps and sunken wreckage along the shoreline offer prime opportunities to track clandestine Defias cargo and slip past the territory's violent Mirefin sentinels."},kw={"alcaz island","defias","dreadmurk shore","dustwallow marsh","mirefin","murloc","shipwreck","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","topic:murloc","zone:barrens"},src={"Dreadmurk Shore"}}
E["subzone:dustwallow-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwallow Bay",z="dustwallow",s="Dustwallow Bay is an inlet of the Great Sea tucked between the sodden coast of Dustwallow Marsh and the fortified port of Theramore Isle. Its brackish coastal shallows teem with marine life, treacherous shoals, and secluded coves just off the main maritime routes of eastern Kalimdor.",h="Dustwallow Bay is an inlet of the Great Sea tucked between the sodden coast of Dustwallow Marsh and the...",sec={{t="Waters of the Eastern Marsh",b="Dustwallow Bay defines the coastal boundary where the stagnant, murky wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh meet the open waters of the Great Sea. Flanked to the east by Theramore Isle, the bay serves as an oceanic approach for vessels arriving at Lady Jaina Proudmoore's island haven. Despite heavy maritime traffic running to and from the docks, the surrounding coastline remains wild and hazardous, pocked with rocky outcrops, murloc encampments, and tucked-away inlets like Tidefury Cove.",sp=0},{t="A Fisherman's Haven",b="While the marsh itself is infested with crocolisks and hostile beasts, the bay's islands and inlets draw those who seek isolation and rich catches. The small islets dotting the waters near Tidefury Cove provide a secluded retreat for anglers, most notably the legendary fisherman Nat Pagle, who can often be found angling off the rocks away from the bustling city of Theramore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwallow Bay located?",a="Dustwallow Bay lies along the eastern coastline of central Kalimdor. It sits directly between the sodden eastern shores of Dustwallow Marsh and the rocky citadel of Theramore Isle.",al={"dustwallow bay location","where is dustwallow bay","dustwallow water"}},{q="Who can be found in the bay?",a="The most famous resident of the bay's outer reaches is Nat Pagle, the world-renowned angler. He makes his camp on a small islet tucked into nearby Tidefury Cove, just southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"who is in dustwallow bay","nat pagle dustwallow bay","npcs dustwallow bay"}},{q="Is Dustwallow Bay safe to swim across?",a="While the bay is relatively close to the safety of Theramore Isle, its shallows and coastlines are frequented by murlocs, sharks, and other aggressive aquatic wildlife native to the marsh fringes.",al={"is dustwallow bay dangerous","monsters in dustwallow bay"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance sailors and travelers bound for Kalimdor, Dustwallow Bay is the final stretch of open sea before entering the fortified harbor of Theramore Isle."},kw={"dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","great sea","nat pagle","theramore","tidefury cove"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:tidefury-cove","npc:nat-pagle"},src={"Dustwallow Bay"}}
E["subzone:foothold-citadel"] = {t="subzone",n="Foothold Citadel",z="dustwallow",s="At Foothold Citadel, Theramore's guards prepare to defend the island. The fortress holds the Alliance command and barracks on Theramore Isle, overlooking the settlement.",h="At Foothold Citadel, Theramore's guards prepare to defend the island.",sec={{t="Heart of the Theramore Guard",b="Foothold Citadel holds the Alliance defense within Theramore Isle's stone walls. Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul lead the Theramore Guard from its halls. Field medics, logistics officers and quartermasters work beside them. Guards patrol and drill, preparing Lady Jaina Proudmoore's forces for threats from the surrounding swamplands.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Admiral's Fall",b="Foothold Citadel recalls the early days of Theramore. Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized the city to wage his personal crusade against the Horde, and the fortress became the place of his final stand. Thrall's allied force broke through the citadel under Rexxar, a half-ogre warrior, and struck down the Admiral. The fortress has been repaired, though the bloody conflict is remembered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Foothold Citadel used for?",a="Foothold Citadel is the Theramore Guard's headquarters and barracks. Command officers, tactical planners, training facilities and logistics staff work there, along with the local paymaster and medical personnel.",al={"foothold citadel purpose","theramore barracks","what is this building"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="During the conflict after the Third War, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore seized Theramore to wage war on the young Horde. A combined force led by the champion Rexxar stormed the citadel and killed the Admiral in his own headquarters.",al={"daelin death","daelin proudmoore last stand","who killed daelin"}},{q="Who is currently in charge at Foothold Citadel?",a="Captain Garran Vimes and Commander Samaul oversee the garrison's daily patrols and regional security under Lady Jaina Proudmoore's authority.",al={"who leads the citadel","theramore guard commander","citadel leader"}},{q="Can I receive medical aid inside the citadel?",a="Yes. Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen lives inside Foothold Citadel. He tends wounded guardsmen and teaches Alliance travelers advanced field medicine and triage.",al={"citadel doctor","theramore medic","first aid trainer theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Foothold Citadel is the Alliance's main military post in southern Kalimdor. Its officers coordinate defense against swamp beasts, Grimtotem marauders and watchful Horde scouts.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde remembers Foothold Citadel as the place where Rexxar and Thrall ended Grand Admiral Proudmoore's campaign to protect Durotar."},kw={"barracks","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","foothold citadel","garran vimes","gustaf vanhowzen","samaul","theramore"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","topic:alliance","npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","npc:thrall"},src={"Foothold Citadel"}}
E["subzone:lost-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Lost Point",z="dustwallow",s="Lost Point is a dilapidated wooden watchtower standing in western Dustwallow Marsh, originally constructed by Theramore's forces as an advance scout post. It has since fallen into disrepair and slipped from the control of Lady Jaina Proudmoore's guard, now serving as a hideout for rogue deserters.",h="Lost Point is a dilapidated wooden watchtower standing in western Dustwallow Marsh, originally constructed by...",sec={{t="A Forsaken Outpost",b="Erected by the expeditionary forces of Theramore to monitor traffic and threats emerging from the Barrens, Lost Point has long outlived its intended military function. The outpost has decayed under the relentless moisture of the marsh, its timber rotting and its defenses abandoned by regular troops. Instead of garrison sentries, the tower and its immediate surroundings are occupied by human deserters who broke away from Theramore's service, finding shelter in the isolated wilderness far from the discipline of the city's commanders.",sp=0},{t="Den of Deserters",b="The deserters ensconced at Lost Point answer to Balos Jacken, a disgruntled former soldier who has banded these rogues together. Their presence is far more than a simple matter of military insubordination. Jacken and his cohorts hold key testimonies regarding traitorous elements within Theramore's ranks, including the involvement of Private Hendel in a high-stakes conspiracy that reaches into the upper echelons of the Alliance.",sp=1,bt={"q1274.5"}}},faq={{q="What is Lost Point?",a="Lost Point is a rundown watchtower built by the humans of Theramore in the western marshes of Dustwallow. Though meant to serve as an advance scout tower, it has been abandoned by the military and taken over by deserters.",al={"lost point overview","what is this tower","about lost point"}},{q="Who lives at Lost Point right now?",a="The tower and surrounding camp are currently inhabited by Theramore deserters. These renegade human soldiers have abandoned their oaths to Theramore and operate under the leadership of Balos Jacken.",al={"who is at lost point","lost point enemies","lost point mobs"}},{q="Who is Balos Jacken?",a="Balos Jacken is the ringleader of the Theramore deserters hiding at Lost Point. Despite his criminal standing, he possesses crucial intelligence about troubling matters within Theramore's ranks.",al={"balos jacken","deserter leader","who leads lost point"},sp=1},{q="Why did Theramore abandon the tower?",a="Dustwallow Marsh is hostile and difficult to supply. As garrison morale broke and discipline strained, the isolated outpost fell into disrepair, becoming an ideal sanctuary for soldiers seeking to escape duty without fleeing into Horde territory.",al={"why abandoned","why is lost point ruined","why run down"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance loyalists, Lost Point is a bitter symbol of fraying discipline within Theramore's ranks and a den of renegades harboring dark secrets about military treason."},kw={"balos jacken","dustwallow marsh","lost point","scout tower","theramore deserters"},rel={"zone:dustwallow"},src={"Lost Point"}}
E["subzone:nat-s-landing"] = {t="subzone",n="Nat's Landing",z="dustwallow",s="Nat's Landing is a modest fishing outpost nestled along the shores of Dustwallow Bay in Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the personal camp and retreat of Nat Pagle, widely regarded as the most famous angler on Azeroth. Adventurers from across the world seek out this humble dock to hone their mastery of the fishing craft.",h="Nat's Landing is a modest fishing outpost nestled along the shores of Dustwallow Bay in Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Master's Haven",b="Tucked away southwest of Theramore Isle along the murky waters of Dustwallow Bay, Nat's Landing is little more than a weathered campsite. It consists of a simple canvas tent, drying racks heavy with the day's catch, extra tackle hung from trees, and a rickety wooden pier jutting into the bay. Despite the mists and hazards of the swamp, this quiet patch of shoreline provides the legendary angler Nat Pagle with a solitary place to cast his line and enjoy a quiet drink away from civilization's clamor.",sp=0},{t="The Fisherman's Pilgrimage",b="Though unassuming at a glance, the landing is an essential stop for aspiring anglers. Fishermen who have exhausted the teachings of standard trainers in Ironforge, Orgrimmar, or elsewhere are directed here to prove their worth directly to Nat. Pagle cares nothing for politics or factional squabbles; any angler who braves the marshland predators to reach his dock must demonstrate patience and skill across the world's most perilous waters to earn his highest instruction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nat's Landing located?",a="Nat's Landing is situated on a small coastal outcrop along the waters of Dustwallow Bay, in the eastern stretches of Dustwallow Marsh just southwest of Theramore Isle.",al={"where is nats landing","nats landing location","how to get to nats landing"}},{q="Who lives at Nat's Landing?",a="The landing is the personal campsite of Nat Pagle, the renowned human angler who spends his days fishing off the pier with a drink in hand.",al={"who is at nats landing","nats landing npc","who lives here"}},{q="Why do anglers travel here?",a="When anglers have mastered all their local trainers can teach them in major capitals, they are sent to Nat Pagle. He tests their dedication with challenging catches around the world before granting them artisan-level instruction.",al={"why come to nats landing","artisan fishing trainer","nat pagle training"}},{q="Does Nat Pagle welcome both Alliance and Horde?",a="Yes. Nat Pagle is neutral toward dedicated anglers, welcoming both Alliance travelers from Theramore and Horde travelers venturing in from the Barrens, regardless of faction loyalties.",al={"is nats landing hostile","can horde talk to nat","is nat pagle neutral"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance citizens stationed in Theramore, Nat's Landing is a short, quiet walk down the coast, offering easy access to the world's premier fisherman.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde anglers trekking across the perilous swamp from the Barrens will find Nat indifferent to the war, judging visitors solely by the quality of their cast."},kw={"angler","dock","dustwallow bay","dustwallow marsh","fishing","nat pagle","nats landing","theramore"},rel={"npc:nat-pagle","zone:dustwallow","subzone:dustwallow-bay","quest:6608","subzone:zul-gurub","zone:ironforge","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Nat's Landing"}}
E["subzone:onyxia-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Onyxia's Lair",z="dustwallow",s="Onyxia's Lair is a subterranean cavern located deep within the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the nesting sanctuary and stronghold for Onyxia, broodmother of the black dragonflight. Inside its sweltering, magma-filled chambers, the great dragon watches over clutches of black dragon eggs.",h="Onyxia's Lair is a subterranean cavern located deep within the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="A Den of Magma and Ruin",b="Carved into the treacherous mud and petrified wood of the Wyrmbog, the cavern entrance resembles the yawning maw of a dragon. Within, the cool rot of the marsh gives way to intense volcanic heat. Magma seeps from cracks in the obsidian stone, while subterranean tremors routinely shake the ceilings. The central chamber opens into a vast incubator where hundreds of black dragon eggs lie nested amid ash and embers, overseen by flightkin, dragonspawn guards, and Onyxia herself.",sp=0},{t="The Broodmother's Retreat",b="While Onyxia's brother Nefarian plots across the sea from Blackrock Spire, Onyxia has long maintained this secluded roost on Kalimdor to breed the next generation of the black dragonflight. The lair acts as a redoubt when her intricate political schemes unravel. Here, far from the courts of mortal kingdoms, she can abandon her human guises and take her true, terrible form as daughter of Deathwing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Onyxia's Lair?",a="The lair is situated in southern Dustwallow Marsh within the Wyrmbog, just south of the Dragonmurk. The entrance is marked by massive dragon bones, smoldering terrain, and black dragonkin sentries guarding a stony fissure shaped like an open jaw.",al={"where is onyxia","onyxia location","how to find onyxia lair","dragonmurk cave"}},{q="What creatures dwell inside the lair?",a="The cavern is inhabited almost entirely by members of the black dragonflight. Broodmother Onyxia commands the deep chamber, surrounded by swarms of freshly hatched whelps, guardian dragonspawn, and mature black drakes.",al={"onyxia lair mobs","who lives in onyxia lair","what is inside"}},{q="Why is the cave so hot if it sits in a swamp?",a="Onyxia dug her lair deep into Kalimdor's crust, tapping into subterranean veins of magma. The extreme volcanic heat provides the scorching conditions necessary to incubate black dragon eggs, contrasting sharply with the cold mud of Dustwallow Marsh above.",al={"why is there lava in dustwallow","onyxia lair volcano"}},{q="Why is Onyxia hiding out in Kalimdor?",a="Dustwallow Marsh offers isolation and concealment. Its thick fogs, dismal quagmires, and dangerous wildlife keep mortal armies away, allowing the broodmother to replenish her flight's numbers undisturbed while she coordinates her covert meddling abroad.",al={"why is onyxia here","why dustwallow marsh","onyxia kalimdor"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, this cavern is the den of a black broodmother whose growing brood threatens Theramore and every settlement around the marsh.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwallow Marsh borders Horde territory in the Barrens and Mulgore; allowing a black broodmother to hatch an army of dragons on Kalimdor poses an existential threat to all of the new Horde."},kw={"black dragonflight","broodmother","dragonmurk","dustwallow","lair","onyxia","whelps","wyrmbog"},rel={"npc:onyxia","subzone:dragonmurk","zone:dustwallow","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:wyrmbog","npc:deathwing","zone:stormwind"},src={"Onyxia's Lair"}}
E["subzone:quagmire"] = {t="subzone",n="Quagmire",z="dustwallow",s="The Quagmire comprises the sprawling, treacherous heart of central Dustwallow Marsh. Bound by Brackenwall Village to the north and the Dragonmurk to the south, its waterlogged flats are notoriously difficult to navigate. Hostile beasts and ravenous oozes make any journey through this central fen perilous.",h="The Quagmire comprises the sprawling, treacherous heart of central Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Heart of the Fen",b="Occupying the wide expanse between Lost Point in the west and Dustwallow Bay in the east, the Quagmire represents the wild core of the marsh. Footing is unreliable at best, with solid earth constantly giving way to murky water and clinging mud. Travelers must contend with predatory crocolisks lurking beneath the scum, aggressive spiders nesting in the dead brush, and strange oozes that seep through the muck.",sp=0},{t="Encroaching Clashes",b="Beyond its natural hazards, the Quagmire serves as an unpredictable crossroads for the sentient powers contesting the swamp. Tucked away within the bog lies Tabetha's Farm, a lonely refuge for practitioners seeking hermit wisdom amid the dangers of the swamp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Quagmire located?",a="The Quagmire covers the central portion of Dustwallow Marsh. It stretches west toward Lost Point, east toward Dustwallow Bay, north to the borders of Brackenwall Village, and south where the land descends into the Dragonmurk.",al={"quagmire location","where is the quagmire","quagmire map"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Deep in the fen lies Tabetha's Farm, a vital destination for aspiring mages seeking esoteric training far from the scrutiny of the Kirin Tor."},kw={"beezil","crocolisk","dustwallow","quagmire","tabetha"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","subzone:beezil-s-wreck","subzone:lost-point","topic:tauren"},src={"Quagmire"}}
E["subzone:sentry-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Sentry Point",z="dustwallow",s="Sentry Point is a human watchtower stationed on the mainland edge of Dustwallow Marsh, guarding the causeway bridge that leads directly to Theramore Isle. Maintained by Theramore's forces, it monitors traffic entering and exiting Lady Jaina Proudmoore's island citadel.",h="Sentry Point is a human watchtower stationed on the mainland edge of Dustwallow Marsh, guarding the causeway...",sec={{t="The Gates of Theramore",b="Positioned at the western end of the long bridge linking Theramore Isle to the treacherous wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh, Sentry Point serves as the stronghold's first line of defense on the mainland. The stone scout tower keeps watch over the swamp road, ensuring that hostile marsh beasts or Horde raiders cannot approach the island city unnoticed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sentry Point used for?",a="It serves as an early warning post and border checkpoint for Theramore Isle. The guards stationed here monitor traffic traveling the swamp road and alert the city guards to approaching threats.",al={"sentry point purpose","what is this tower","why is sentry point here"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The outpost is manned and maintained by the Theramore Guard, operating under the command of Lady Jaina Proudmoore and her military officers.",al={"who owns sentry point","is sentry point alliance","theramore guard tower"}},{q="Is Sentry Point safe for Horde travelers?",a="No. While Lady Jaina Proudmoore strives for peace with the Horde, the military guards stationed at this outpost protect Alliance territory and will attack trespassing Horde members on sight.",al={"can horde go to sentry point","horde friendly sentry point"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers coming from the perilous bogs of Dustwallow Marsh, Sentry Point marks the welcoming threshold to the safety of Theramore Isle.",["faction:Horde"]="The tower serves as a stark reminder of Theramore's military presence on the Kalimdor mainland, heavily guarded against any approaching Horde scouts."},kw={"bridge","dustwallow marsh","guard tower","jaina proudmoore","sentry point","theramore","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Sentry Point"}}
E["subzone:shady-rest-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Shady Rest Inn",z="dustwallow",s="The Shady Rest Inn was once a welcoming human-built waystation sitting just off the road between the Barrens and Theramore Isle. Today, only charred timbers and smoldering ashes remain following a sudden and violent arson attack. The tragedy left the innkeeper shattered and sparked tension across the marsh as investigators sift through the wreckage for clues.",h="The Shady Rest Inn was once a welcoming human-built waystation sitting just off the road between the Barrens...",sec={{t="Ashes on the Border",b="Built to serve travelers navigating the treacherous crossing between Dustwallow Marsh and the Barrens, the Shady Rest Inn stood as an outpost of civilized comfort in a harsh wilderness. That ended when the inn was abruptly razed to the ground in a devastating fire. Innkeeper James Hyal managed to survive the inferno, but the blaze claimed the lives of his wife and child. Traumatized and grief-stricken, Hyal was left with nothing as the ruins became an active crime scene, drawing scrutiny from Theramore authorities desperate to identify who ignited the flames.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Suspicion",b="Initial inquiries into the arson pointed toward human deserters and suspicious soldiers, with figures such as Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell falling under heavy suspicion before meeting untimely ends. However, physical evidence recovered from the ashes—including distinctive hoofprints and ritual badges—revealed that the attack was not merely an act of internal treachery. The arson was carried out by the ruthless Grimtotem tauren, who strike from the deep marsh to sow discord between Theramore and its neighbors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the Shady Rest Inn?",a="The inn was attacked and burned to the ground. Deserters and rogue Alliance soldiers were initially suspected, and investigators are still sifting the ashes for clues to who was truly behind the arson.",al={"why is shady rest inn burned","what happened to the inn","who burned shady rest"},sp=1},{q="Who owned and operated the inn?",a="James Hyal ran the Shady Rest Inn. He survived the blaze, but his wife and child perished in the flames, leaving him deeply traumatized.",al={"innkeeper shady rest","who ran shady rest","james hyal"}},{q="Where is the Shady Rest Inn located?",a="The ruins lie along the main road in western Dustwallow Marsh, right near the border where the marsh gives way to the Barrens.",al={"shady rest location","where is shady rest inn"}},{q="Who are Paval Reethe and Lieutenant Caldwell?",a="They were human suspects implicated during the early investigation into the fire. Both died before investigators could extract confessions or definitively uncover the full extent of their involvement.",al={"who is reethe","lieutenant caldwell shady rest","reethe and caldwell"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The destruction of the inn represents a severe security breach on the main overland route to Theramore Isle, threatening travelers and inflaming fears of hidden enemies.",["race:Tauren"]="Suspicion over who burned the inn threatens to shatter the fragile peace between the Horde and Jaina Proudmoore's forces in Dustwallow Marsh."},kw={"arson","barrens border","dustwallow marsh","grimtotem","james hyal","paval reethe","shady rest inn","theramore"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","topic:tauren"},src={"Shady Rest Inn"}}
E["subzone:stonemaul-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonemaul Ruins",z="dustwallow",s="The Stonemaul Ruins are the shattered remnants of Stonemaul Village, once the proud Kalimdor settlement of the Stonemaul ogres. After being driven out by the black dragonflight, the clan fled north, leaving their former home overrun by Firemane dragonspawn.",h="The Stonemaul Ruins are the shattered remnants of Stonemaul Village, once the proud Kalimdor settlement of...",sec={{t="Rise and Fall of the Clan Home",b="Following their migration to Kalimdor, the Stonemaul ogres founded their settlement amid the murky swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. The village became famous when the beastmaster Rexxar braved the clan's lethal trials, slew their brutal chieftain Kor'gall, and rallied the ogres to defend the nascent Horde against Admiral Proudmoore's forces. After the war, Rexxar left the ogre Mok'Morokk in command. Under Mok'Morokk's selfish rule, the village fell into decline and was ultimately ambushed and shattered by the black dragonflight. The surviving ogres fled north to establish Brackenwall Village, while Onyxia's brood took complete possession of the ruins.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Reclamation",b="Today, the ruins are firmly ensconced within Dragonmurk and crawl with Firemane dragonspawn tending the brood's nearby nesting grounds. While Overlord Mok'Morokk grew cowardly and content to languish in Brackenwall, older and prouder clan members like Tharg and Draz'Zilb refuse to abandon their homeland. Operating out of Brackenwall, they urge Horde champions to slaughter the occupying dragonspawn and smash the dragonflight's eggs in hopes that the Stonemaul may one day march back and reclaim their ancestral village.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who used to live in Stonemaul Ruins?",a="The Stonemaul clan of ogres built and inhabited the settlement, then known as Stonemaul Village, after arriving on Kalimdor.",al={"who lived here","stonemaul ruins history","who built stonemaul village"}},{q="Why was the village abandoned?",a="Onyxia's black dragonflight assaulted the settlement and drove the ogres out, turning the village into a nesting outpost for Firemane dragonspawn.",al={"why is stonemaul destroyed","what happened to stonemaul village","who attacked stonemaul"}},{q="Where did the surviving ogres go?",a="The survivors retreated north into Dustwallow Marsh under Overlord Mok'Morokk and established Brackenwall Village as their temporary stronghold.",al={"where are the ogres now","stonemaul ogre location"}},{q="What was Rexxar's connection to this place?",a="Rexxar came here to enlist the ogres against Kul Tiras. He bested their trial, slew their tyrannical warlord Kor'gall in combat, and briefly served as chieftain before passing leadership to Mok'Morokk.",al={"rexxar stonemaul","rexxar ogre chieftain"}},{q="Do the ogres plan to retake the ruins?",a="Yes. While Mok'Morokk was afraid to act, other Stonemaul leaders like Tharg and Draz'Zilb actively recruit Horde adventurers to culled the Firemane dragonspawn and prepare for retaking their home.",al={"will the ogres go back","retaking stonemaul"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Stonemaul ogres are staunch allies who shed blood alongside Thrall's Horde against Kul Tiras. Helping them strike back against the black dragonflight honors that pact."},kw={"brackenwall","dragonmurk","firemane","kor'gall","mok'morokk","stonemaul","stonemaul ruins","stonemaul village"},rel={"subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:dragonmurk","npc:overlord-mok-morokk","npc:onyxia","topic:black-dragonflight","topic:horde","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Stonemaul Ruins"}}
E["subzone:swamplight-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Swamplight Manor",z="dustwallow",s="Swamplight Manor is an ironically named, ramshackle wooden shack nestled deep within Witch Hill in Dustwallow Marsh. It serves as the eccentric home and kitchen of 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, an isolated recluse known across the mire for his strange culinary appetites. Despite its humble, eerie isolation, the surrounding garden conceals intrigue that catches the attention of both Theramore and Brackenwall Village.",h="Swamplight Manor is an ironically named, ramshackle wooden shack nestled deep within Witch Hill in Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Respite in the Mire",b="Despite what its grandiose title suggests, Swamplight Manor is far from a lordly estate. It is merely a crooked, weather-beaten shack tucked into the haunted wetlands of Witch Hill. Its lone resident, the odd recluse known as 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, lives a solitary existence surrounded by fog, muck, and restless marsh ghosts. Jarl spends his days concocting unusual regional delicacies out of local wildlife, frequently recruiting wandering adventurers to hunt down bizarre ingredients like marsh frog legs and creature eyes to satisfy his strange craft.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Garden",b="While travelers usually stumble upon the manor seeking eccentric cooking or shelter from the spirits of Witch Hill, the grounds conceal a much darker border conflict. Buried under a loose pile of dirt in Jarl's makeshift garden lies a discarded orcish spy's report, complete with a severed head nearby. Both the Theramore guards under Captain Garran Vimes and the Horde forces at Brackenwall Village have keen interests in recovering these documents, making the hermit's patch of overgrown soil an unexpected flashpoint in the regional cold war.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a tiny shack called a 'Manor'?",a="The name is purely ironic. The structure is little more than a soggy, rundown wooden hovel, named with a touch of eccentricity by its reclusive inhabitant, 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, to contrast with the dreary gloom of Witch Hill.",al={"swamplight manor name origin","why manor","is swamplight a real manor"}},{q="Who lives at Swamplight Manor?",a="'Swamp Eye' Jarl lives here alone. He is an infamous, half-crazed hermit and cook who chooses to dwell isolated in the haunted mire, hiring passing travelers to supply him with peculiar culinary ingredients and aid with the local spirits.",al={"who is swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor resident","who lives here"}},{q="What is buried in the garden outside?",a="Hidden in a pile of disturbed earth in Jarl's yard is a lost spy report penned by an orc, along with a severed head. Both Alliance authorities in Theramore and Horde scouts from Brackenwall Village are anxious to secure this intelligence.",al={"swamplight manor dirt pile","loose dirt swamplight","orc spy report"},sp=1},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde players visit Jarl?",a="Yes. Jarl lives so far removed from civilization that he maintains neutrality, gladly accepting help or trading recipes with both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"is jarl neutral","can horde talk to swamp eye jarl","swamplight faction"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For culinarians braving the marshlands, Jarl represents the eccentric pinnacle of swamp foraging, crafting regional meals out of creatures most chefs would dread to touch.",["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore scouts sent by Captain Garran Vimes keep a watchful eye on rumors surrounding the manor, particularly concerning missing scouts and intercepted Horde correspondence."},kw={"brackenwall village","dustwallow marsh","garran vimes","lost report","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"subzone:witch-hill","zone:dustwallow","subzone:brackenwall-village","quest:165","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Swamplight Manor"}}
E["subzone:tabetha-s-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tabetha's Farm",z="dustwallow",s="Deep in the murkiest reaches of the Quagmire lies Tabetha's Farm, an isolated homestead centered around a small wooden hut, a modest garden, and a private dock. Despite the treacherous marsh surroundings, this sanctuary serves as a hidden redoubt for the hermit mage Tabetha.",h="Deep in the murkiest reaches of the Quagmire lies Tabetha's Farm, an isolated homestead centered around a...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Sanctuary",b="Tucked away in the western wetlands of Dustwallow Marsh, Tabetha's Farm defies its unforgiving environment. Consisting of a weather-worn hut, small vegetable plots, and a dock for navigating the swamp's murky waterways, the homestead offers a quiet refuge far from the political rivalries of Theramore and Brackenwall Village. Here, the reclusive human sorceress Tabetha lives in near-total seclusion, pursuing esoteric studies of arcane and fel power without interference from Dalaran or local authorities.",sp=0},{t="A Waypoint of Arcane Power",b="Despite its remote location, the farm attracts practitioners of the magical arts from across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Mages seeking mastery over raw arcane surges and warlocks seeking aid to cleanse volatile artifacts like the Orb of Orahil are directed to Tabetha's doorstep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Tabetha's Farm?",a="The farm is home to the eccentric mage Tabetha, who keeps the small garden, dock, and homestead amidst the perilous swamp creatures of the Quagmire.",al={"who is tabetha","who lives here","inhabitants of tabetha's farm"}},{q="Why do mages travel all the way to this farm?",a="Mage trainers across the world direct promising students to Tabetha to further their arcane knowledge. She possesses deep expertise regarding volatile mana surges, ancient relics, and primal powers that standard city academies rarely teach.",al={"why do mages visit tabetha","mage quest dustwallow","mage class quest tabetha"}},{q="Why would warlocks come here?",a="Warlocks seek out Tabetha's expertise in exorcism and elemental energies when working to purify and tame dangerous artifacts, most notably during the rituals required to cleanse the Orb of Orahil.",al={"tabetha warlock quest","cleansing orb of orahil","warlock tabetha"}},{q="Is Tabetha's Farm allied with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Tabetha maintains a neutral stance, offering her wisdom to travelers regardless of their political allegiance. Her farm remains independent of both Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore and the Horde forces at Brackenwall Village.",al={"is tabetha alliance","is tabetha horde","is tabetha neutral"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Your trainers in the capital cities hold Tabetha's esoteric knowledge in high esteem, sending adept spellcasters to her farm to investigate volatile mana surges and ancient relics of power.",["class:Warlock"]="Though she lives as a quiet swamp hermit, Tabetha is one of the few spellcasters capable of assisting you in cleansing the potent energies bound to the Orb of Orahil."},kw={"dustwallow","dustwallow marsh","quagmire","tabetha","tabetha's farm","tabetha's hut"},rel={"npc:tabetha","subzone:quagmire","zone:dustwallow","quest:2300","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Tabetha's Farm"}}
E["subzone:theramore-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Theramore Isle",z="dustwallow",s="Theramore Isle shelters refugees from Lordaeron behind the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh. Lady Jaina Proudmoore founded the fortified port, now the Alliance's chief stronghold in southern Kalimdor.",h="Theramore Isle shelters refugees from Lordaeron behind the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh.",sec={{t="Refuge of the West",b="After the Scourge ravaged Dalaran and Lordaeron in the Third War, Lady Jaina Proudmoore led survivors across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. There, humans, dwarves, and high elves fought beside orcs and night elves to defeat the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal.\n\nAfter the victory, Jaina's coalition withdrew to the misty edge of Dustwallow Marsh. On an island just off the coast, they raised a harbor city with stone ramparts and Jaina's citadel, sheltering what remained of the northern kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="An Uneasy Peace",b="Theramore's peace with Thrall's Horde in neighboring Durotar has long been uneasy. When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore arrived with the Kul Tiras fleet, he took command of the isle and began a campaign against the orcs.\n\nJaina would not let hatred undo Kalimdor's hard-won survival. She allowed the Horde to kill her father within Theramore's walls to preserve the peace. The city now holds a fragile truce with Durotar, though veteran sailors' resentment threatens to break it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Theramore Isle?",a="Lady Jaina Proudmoore governs Theramore Isle. A master sorceress from Dalaran and Kul Tiras, she led Lordaeron's survivors to Kalimdor during the Third War. She oversees the city's defenses and diplomacy.",al={"who leads theramore","theramore ruler","jaina theramore"}},{q="Why did humans build a city in a swamp?",a="After the Battle of Mount Hyjal, the surviving human expedition needed a defensible coast to shelter its people and keep a navy. The rocky island off Dustwallow Marsh offered deep-water anchorage and separation from mainland threats, despite the bog surrounding it.",al={"why dustwallow","why is theramore in a marsh","why build here"}},{q="Is Theramore hostile to the Horde?",a="Theramore is an Alliance stronghold, and its guards meet Horde travelers with hostility. Yet Lady Jaina Proudmoore and Warchief Thrall keep an uneasy peace and respect each other's borders, despite lingering hatred among their people.",al={"can horde visit theramore","theramore horde relations","are theramore humans at war"}},{q="What happened to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore here?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore took Theramore from his daughter Jaina to make war on the young Horde. Seeing that his campaign would destroy them all, Jaina stepped aside as Thrall and Rexxar stormed the citadel and killed the Admiral in battle.",al={"daelin death","what happened to jaina's father","daelin proudmoore theramore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Theramore Isle is the Alliance's chief seat of power in central Kalimdor. It offers safety, ferry connections, and a defended harbor amid hostile wilderness.",["class:Mage"]="As Archmage Jaina Proudmoore's home, Theramore holds powerful arcane conduits. It is a vital center of Kirin Tor tradition and teleportation in the western hemisphere."},kw={"alliance","daelin proudmoore","dustwallow marsh","jaina proudmoore","kul tiras","lordaeron refugees","theramore"},rel={"npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:dustwallow","topic:kul-tiras","npc:thrall","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:ratchet"},src={"Theramore Isle"}}
E["subzone:tidefury-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Tidefury Cove",z="dustwallow",s="Tidefury Cove is a treacherous stretch of water and rocky shallows along the southeastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, south of Theramore Isle. Renowned for its hazardous reefs and wrecked vessels, it serves as a secluded haven for roaming makrura and solitary anglers.",h="Tidefury Cove is a treacherous stretch of water and rocky shallows along the southeastern coast of Dustwallow...",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships and Reefs",b="Tucked away at the far end of Dustwallow Bay between Theramore Isle and the Wyrmbog, Tidefury Cove presents a notorious navigational hazard to passing sailors. Jagged reefs and shifting shoals have claimed multiple vessels over the years, leaving rotting wooden hulks half-submerged in the tideline. Today, the ruined ships are crawled over by opportunistic makrura, turning the cove into a dangerous, isolated stretch of coastline visited mostly by hardy scavengers or quiet hermits seeking distance from Theramore's busy docks.",sp=0},{t="The Historic Foothold",b="During the invasion of Durotar, the shores of Tidefury Cove became a crucial strategic battleground. Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiran expedition fortified the coast with an imposing coastal fortress and guard towers to command the approaches to Theramore. To break Proudmoore's grip, Thrall marshaled the combined strength of the young Horde—uniting orcs, Darkspear trolls, and tauren alongside Rexxar and the Stonemaul ogres—to storm the shoreline and dismantle the Kul Tiran beachhead before pressing directly toward the island fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tidefury Cove located?",a="Tidefury Cove sits along the southeastern edge of Dustwallow Marsh, just south of Theramore Isle and bordering the Wyrmbog coast at the southern end of Dustwallow Bay.",al={"tidefury cove location","where is tidefury cove","tidefury cove map"}},{q="Why are there shipwrecks in Tidefury Cove?",a="The cove is filled with shallow sandbars and hidden rocky reefs that make navigation extremely hazardous. Ships that stray too close to the coast frequently run aground, where waves and scavengers quickly reduce them to broken hulls.",al={"tidefury shipwrecks","broken ships tidefury","sunken ships dustwallow bay"}},{q="Who lives in Tidefury Cove today?",a="Aside from aggressive shoreline makrura, the cove's most notable resident is the famed angler Nat Pagle, who maintains an encampment known as Nat's Landing on one of the outer islets.",al={"who is in tidefury cove","tidefury cove residents","nat pagle location"}},{q="What battle took place here in the past?",a="During Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's campaign against the new Horde, Kul Tiran forces built a heavily fortified coastal stronghold here. Thrall's Horde, bolstered by tauren and ogre allies, assaulted and destroyed the base to clear the way to Theramore Isle.",al={"battle of tidefury cove","warcraft 3 tidefury","invasion of durotar tidefury"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this coastline was the launching point for the final counter-offensive that broke Grand Admiral Proudmoore's naval aggression and secured the young nation's survival.",["profession:Cooking"]="The rich coastal shallows and proximity to master angler Nat Pagle make this stretch of Dustwallow a prime destination for fishermen seeking prized catches."},kw={"cove","dustwallow","makrura","pagle","proudmoore","reefs","shipwreck","theramore","tidefury"},rel={"subzone:dustwallow-bay","subzone:nat-s-landing","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:wyrmbog","zone:dustwallow","npc:nat-pagle","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Tidefury Cove"}}
E["subzone:witch-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Witch Hill",z="dustwallow",s="Witch Hill is a dreary, mist-shrouded rise in the heart of Dustwallow Marsh along the path toward Theramore. It is best known for the secluded Swamplight Manor, scattered camps of hostile Mirefin murlocs, and sinister rumors of dark hauntings.",h="Witch Hill is a dreary, mist-shrouded rise in the heart of Dustwallow Marsh along the path toward Theramore.",sec={{t="A Blighted Rise",b="Rising out of the stagnant waters of Dustwallow Marsh, Witch Hill sits roughly a third of the way along the peninsula leading southeast toward Theramore Isle. The elevated ground provides little refuge from the hazards of the swamp, as aggressive Mirefin murlocs claim the surrounding waters. At its center stands Swamplight Manor, the lonely and unsettling residence of the hermit known as 'Swamp Eye' Jarl. Travelers passing through frequently report eerie phenomena and lingering dark presences across the knoll.",sp=0},{t="The Haunting of the Hill",b="Behind its quiet, gloomy exterior, Witch Hill is steeped in dark rumor. Tales of hauntings cling to the desolate ground, adding to the local paranoia. Those who brave the hill must contend not only with the primitive savagery of the Mirefin, but with occult threats that make even seasoned Theramore patrols uneasy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Witch Hill located?",a="Witch Hill is located in Dustwallow Marsh, situated about a third of the way down the peninsula that connects the western marsh to Theramore Isle.",al={"witch hill location","where is witch hill","how to find witch hill"}},{q="Who lives on Witch Hill?",a="The most prominent resident is 'Swamp Eye' Jarl, an eccentric hermit living inside Swamplight Manor near the hill's center. The surrounding lowlands are also infested by camps of Mirefin murlocs.",al={"who lives here","witch hill inhabitants","swamplight manor resident"}},{q="Why is the area called Witch Hill?",a="The knoll has long had a sinister reputation for dark magic, odd lights, and supernatural danger, compounded by the eerie solitude of Swamplight Manor.",al={"why witch hill","is there a witch here","witch hill lore"},sp=1},{q="What threats should travelers look out for on Witch Hill?",a="Travelers must beware of roaming Mirefin murlocs establishing camps around the hill, as well as the unsettling rumors of hauntings that cling to the hill.",al={"witch hill dangers","witch hill enemies","mobs on witch hill"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks passing along the Theramore road may sense the dark rumors of hauntings clinging to the dreary knoll.",["faction:Alliance"]="Witch Hill borders the primary overland route toward Theramore Isle, making its murloc tribes and dark entities an ongoing nuisance for travelers and couriers."},kw={"dustwallow marsh","mirefin","swamp eye jarl","swamplight manor","witch hill"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:swamplight-manor","topic:murloc"},src={"Witch Hill"}}
E["subzone:wyrmbog"] = {t="subzone",n="Wyrmbog",z="dustwallow",s="Wyrmbog is the perilous southern expanse of Dustwallow Marsh, lying just south of the Dragonmurk. Dominated by foul mire and jagged spires of stone, it serves as the staging ground and territorial buffer for the black dragonflight. The caves of ancient wyrms, including the broodmother Onyxia and the elder Emberstrife, are carved directly into its surrounding ridges.",h="Wyrmbog is the perilous southern expanse of Dustwallow Marsh, lying just south of the Dragonmurk.",sec={{t="Heart of the Brood",b="Wyrmbog represents the most heavily infested black dragon territory in southern Kalimdor. Where the open waters of Dustwallow give way to scorched muck and towering bones, whelps and mature drakes patrol the fetid air. The bog is choked with toxic fumes and predatory beasts driven wild by the draconic presence. Travelers foolish enough to wander into these reaches find themselves directly in the shadow of Onyxia's Lair and Emberstrife's cavernous den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Wyrmbog?",a="Wyrmbog is the treacherous southern region of Dustwallow Marsh, situated south of the Dragonmurk. It is heavily infested with members of the black dragonflight.",al={"wyrmbog","what is wyrmbog","where is wyrmbog"}},{q="Which dragons dwell in Wyrmbog?",a="The black dragonflight commands the territory. Numerous black dragonkin, drakes, and whelps patrol the marsh, while elder wyrms like Emberstrife and the broodmother Onyxia keep their lairs along its southern perimeter.",al={"who lives in wyrmbog","dragons in wyrmbog","what dragons are here"}},{q="Where is Onyxia's Lair located in relation to Wyrmbog?",a="The entrance to Onyxia's Lair is nestled into the rocky spires and cavern openings along the southern edge of the Wyrmbog.",al={"onyxia lair location","where is onyxia","entrance to onyxia"}},{q="Who is Emberstrife?",a="Emberstrife is an ancient black dragon who resides in a cave carved into the rock formations of the Wyrmbog, acting as a powerful guardian within the broodmother's territory.",al={"emberstrife","who is emberstrife","emberstrifes den"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions hunting the black dragonflight, Wyrmbog is the final, treacherous staging ground before reaching Onyxia's threshold.",["faction:Horde"]="Warchief Thrall's scouts keep a wary eye on Wyrmbog, knowing the black dragons nesting so close to the Barrens and Theramore pose a threat to the fragile balance in Kalimdor."},kw={"black dragonflight","dragonmurk","drakes","dustwallow","emberstrife","marsh","onyxia","wyrmbog"},rel={"zone:dustwallow","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:dragonmurk","topic:black-dragonflight","npc:onyxia"},src={"Wyrmbog"}}
E["zone:dustwallow"] = {t="zone",n="Dustwallow Marsh",z="dustwallow",s="Dustwallow Marsh is a vast, sweltering swampland in central Kalimdor, trapped between the arid plains of the Barrens and the Great Sea. Fed by perpetual subterranean springs, its treacherous fens harbor dangerous predators, covert faction skirmishes, and the lurking presence of the black dragonflight. It serves as home to the Alliance fortress-island of Theramore in the east and the Horde-allied Stonemaul ogres of Brackenwall Village to the northwest.",h="Dustwallow Marsh is a vast, sweltering swampland in central Kalimdor, trapped between the arid plains of the...",sec={{t="A Drowned Landscape",b="Before the Great Sundering, Dustwallow was a high, grassy plain teeming with herd animals. The cataclysm shattered the valley, causing the water table to rise and drown the earth in endless stagnant pools, mossy shallows, and choking mud. Underground springs ensure the marsh remains perpetually humid and submerged, blanketed in thick fog and infested with crocolisks, raptors, and spiders. Jagged shallows and wandering bogs make travel perilous for any adventurer stepping off the crumbling causeways.",sp=0},{t="Old Hatreds and Uneasy Truces",b="Dustwallow was largely wild until the aftermath of the Third War, when Lady Jaina Proudmoore led human refugees across the sea to establish the citadel of Theramore Isle on its eastern coast. Soon after, Kul Tiran forces under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore waged war against Thrall's fledgling Horde, culminating in bloody battles across the wetlands and the Admiral's defeat. Today, an official armistice exists between Theramore and Orgrimmar, yet tension smolders beneath the surface. Theramore struggles with desertions and sabotage, while spies wage quiet, deadly conflicts across the fens.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Wyrmbog",b="The south of the marsh rises into a jagged, rocky quagmire known as the Dragonmurk and the Wyrmbog. Originally settled by the Stonemaul ogres under the half-ogre champion Rexxar, the area became a graveyard when the black dragonflight violently drove the clan from Stonemaul Village. The displaced ogres fled north to Brackenwall Village under Overlord Mok'Morokk, swearing vengeance. Within these jagged crags lurks Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing, directing her brood and weaving sinister machinations far beyond the swamp.",sp=2}},faq={{q="What is the main Alliance settlement here?",a="The Alliance's presence is centered at Theramore Isle, a fortified city-state situated on a rocky island off the eastern coast. Founded by Lady Jaina Proudmoore following the Third War, it connects to Kalimdor by a narrow roadway and maintains vital ship routes to Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"alliance base dustwallow","where is theramore","human town dustwallow"}},{q="Where can Horde adventurers find refuge in the swamp?",a="Horde travelers make camp at Brackenwall Village in the northwestern reaches of the marsh. The settlement was founded by the Stonemaul clan of ogres, who joined the Horde under Rexxar and opened their gates to orcish and tauren allies.",al={"horde base dustwallow","where is brackenwall","ogre village"}},{q="Why are there so many black dragons in the southern marsh?",a="The southern region, known as the Wyrmbog and Dragonmurk, is the brood grounds and domain of Onyxia, daughter of Deathwing. Her black dragonspawn violently drove out the Stonemaul ogres and turned the rocky outcroppings and deep caves into nests for whelps and drakes.",al={"wyrmbog dragons","why black dragons here","dragonmurk"},sp=2},{q="What happened to the Stonemaul ogres' original home?",a="The Stonemaul ogres originally dwelt peacefully in Stonemaul Village in the southern marsh. However, the black dragonflight launched a devastating assault, slaughtering many and forcing the survivors to flee northwest to Brackenwall Village.",al={"stonemaul ruins","what happened to stonemaul village","old ogre town"}},{q="Who lives in the lonely cottage out in the Quagmire?",a="The cottage belongs to Tabetha, an eccentric and powerful hermit mage living quietly in the depths of the marsh. Arcane practitioners often seek her out for instruction or assistance with cleansing volatile magical relics.",al={"tabetha's farm","tabetha dustwallow","who is the witch in the swamp"}},{q="What is Alcaz Island and who controls it?",a="Alcaz Island is a heavily guarded isle off the northeast coast of the marsh, held by the Strashaz naga and patrolled by dangerous elite defenders, with hydras lurking in the surrounding waters.",al={"alcaz island","island off coast dustwallow","what is on alcaz"},sp=2}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Dustwallow Marsh hosts Theramore Isle, the heart of the Alliance's presence on Kalimdor. Adventurers arriving via Menethil Harbor guard its causeways while untangling a web of deserters and missing envoys.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde emissaries come to support the beleaguered Stonemaul ogres at Brackenwall Village, repelling dragon incursions from the Wyrmbog and keeping a wary eye on human movements from the coast.",["class:Mage"]="Mages are drawn across the fens to Tabetha's Farm in the Quagmire, seeking out the recluse's unique expertise regarding arcane conduits and ancient power sources."},kw={"alcaz","brackenwall","dustwallow","jaina","marsh","onyxia","quagmire","stonemaul","tabetha","theramore","wyrmbog"},rel={"subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:brackenwall-village","subzone:onyxia-s-lair","subzone:wyrmbog","subzone:stonemaul-ruins","subzone:tabetha-s-farm","quest:1241"},src={"Dustwallow Marsh (Classic)","Dustwallow Marsh"}}
